// Yoopanese (U.P. dialect) translation of Snow War tiers 145–288 (array indices 144–287).
window.YOOPER = window.YOOPER || {};
window.YOOPER.SNOW_WAR_TIERS = Object.assign(window.YOOPER.SNOW_WAR_TIERS || {}, {
  "Depots": { label: "Da Depots", desc: "Dey set up forward stores behind every sector, six of 'em holdin' fifteen hundred rounds apiece. Time from askin' to gettin' it at da line drops from twenty-five minutes to four. Two depots sit inside trebuchet range of da other side's works, an' dey get moved after da first one gets hit, at a loss of eleven hundred rounds." },
  "Self-Propelled Spreaders": { label: "Spreaders Dat Push Demselves", desc: "Dey mount da machines on sled frames an' tow 'em with teams, so da drive comes from da tow instead of da operator's legs. Da screw still turns only when da wheels turn, so da old safety behaviour stays just like it was, at ten times da output. A towed unit lays a hundred-and-forty-centimetre swath at a runnin' pace an' takes four people to stop, ya know." },
  "Mobile Batteries": { label: "Da Batteries on Runners", desc: "Dey put da engines on sled runners an' move 'em every night, four to a battery, so no firin' spot gets used twice. Movin' takes twenty minutes an' cuts counter-battery losses by three quarters. Da catch is accuracy: da first shot from a new spot lands sixty feet wide on average, eh." },
  "Forward Works": { label: "Da Forward Works", desc: "Everything out front of da bailey gets rebuilt to da new scale: four outworks a side at sixteen feet long, four feet high an' twenty inches thick, pushed sixty feet out, an' a redoubt fourteen feet across, six and a half feet high an' forty inches thick holdin' eight hundred rounds. Da fieldworks get recut right along with 'em, nine hundred feet of ready position against da old three hundred, worked by thirty-one people over three days, with da sling lanes widened to take engines. Defended depth from da outermost stake to da bailey wall comes out to two hundred and forty feet, which is just inside da range of da heaviest engine dat can reach it." },
  "Snow Citadel": { label: "Da Snow Citadel", desc: "A fortress with a bunch of chambers an' a roof dat actually holds: five rooms across a footprint averagin' thirty-four feet by twenty-two, forty feet on da long way, six feet of headroom in da middle, walls three feet thick. It gets a name, marked right at da door, an' every position on da map gets figured from it. Buildin' it took sixty person-hours. Dey don't give up da inner bailey, dey make it bigger: a hundred and sixty feet of circuit at seven feet high an' thirty-six inches thick, wrappin' sixteen hundred square feet of citadel an' ammo store, for another ninety person-hours. Garrison runs twenty-eight at da complex out of eighty-eight in da whole war." },
  "Citadel Blanketing": { label: "Tuckin' In Da Citadel", desc: "Da whole citadel gets kept under a coat: eleven crews on rotation, every bare surface redone within seventy-two hours of somebody walkin' on it. Dat eats nine tons of moved-around snow a day, none of it new. From da outer works da citadel looks like it's always, somehow, just been snowed on, an' everybody inside knows dat's a political statement, yah." },
  "Conscription": { label: "Da Draft", desc: "Showin' up ain't voluntary anymore. Every house across four blocks gets assessed at one body per two kids, which makes a roll of a hundred and forty. Ya get out of it for an injury, for havin' a workin' woodstove, or if you're one of da eleven crews already servin' engines. About seventy percent actually show." },
  "Heavy Trebuchets": { label: "Da Big Ol' Trebuchets", desc: "Counterweights go up to four hundred pounds of packed snow on frames dat need a crew of nine. Range gets out to four hundred feet an' one shot takes a foot of glazed wall right off da face. Dey build two, an' each one ties up its crew a whole day every time it gets moved." },
  "Standing Army": { label: "Da Standin' Army", desc: "It quits bein' casual once da roster hits ninety across both sides. Dere's four ranks, uniforms made outta scarves, an' a chain of command dat runs every order through one fella. Attendance gets checked every day, an' turnout stays over eighty percent eleven days straight." },
  "Spreader Conscription": { label: "Drafted onto Da Spreaders", desc: "Runnin' a machine stops bein' somethin' ya volunteer for an' starts bein' assigned, four hundred crews called up in a season. Da guild says an untrained guy lays an uneven bed, gets overruled, an' is proven right inside a month when average coverage variation goes from fourteen percent to thirty-one. Trainin' comes back, from da same folks, an' nobody says a word about it." },
  "Officer Corps": { label: "Da Officers", desc: "Givin' orders gets split off from fightin': eleven officers across both sides, an' not one of 'em has thrown a round in nine days. Orders get written down instead of hollered, about thirty a day, a third of 'em battery instructions. Time from decidin' to doin' at da front runs six minutes." },
  "Spreader Clauses": { label: "Da Spreader Clauses", desc: "Da settlements dey work out start havin' terms about machines: how many each side can keep, what ground can get resurfaced, an' a standin' rule against layin' cover where da other side can see it from its works. Dem clauses are more detailed dan da ones about throwin'. Both sides stick to da count, an' neither one sticks to da sight line, eh." },
  "Treaties": { label: "Da Treaties", desc: "Delegations of six draft an' sign formal agreements on flattened cardboard. Dey set boundaries to da foot, ammo limits at three hundred a side, a cap of four engines apiece, an' terms for when da fightin' starts back up. Four of 'em are in force at once, an' two of 'em disagree about da same line." },
  "Indirect Fire": { label: "Shootin' Blind", desc: "Engines get aimed at targets da crews can't even see, worked off corrections a spotter hollers down from da tower. Spottin' to correction takes ninety seconds, an' da hit rate on somethin' ya can't see settles around one in seven. Da back slope of every position turns into a target for da first time." },
  "Border Commission": { label: "Da Border Commission", desc: "A standin' bunch of nine gets seated to figure out what da treaties mean, even from both sides plus one neutral. Dey rule on forty-one disputes in a month, an' folks accept dem rulings in thirty-four. Boundary markers go in every fifty feet across two miles." },
  "Weather Falsification": { label: "Fakin' Da Weather", desc: "Dey use spreadin' big-time to fake a snowfall dat never happened, across nine square miles, to get school called off in a district dat got nuttin'. It works. Da record for dat day reads as a four-inch storm in every local account an' a dry day on every instrument, an' da mismatch still gets cited a thousand years later by both sides for opposite reasons, holy wah." },
  "Total Snow War": { label: "All-Out Snow War", desc: "A campaign across da whole region, seven neighborhoods, with offensives all lined up on one timetable. Da war's gone on nine days longer dan da storm dat started it, with better dan three hundred people in it. Daily use across every front goes past twelve thousand rounds, a third of it thrown by battery — forty engines workin', trebuchets an' torsion onagers in about equal numbers." },
  "Pattern Engines": { label: "Engines Off Da Same Pattern", desc: "Engine buildin' gets standardized to one drawin' — one frame, one arm length, one cup — so parts off any wreck fit any engine still standin'. Dey build ninety to da pattern in a month, against forty of mixed design still in service. Time to get a busted engine back on da line drops from two days to four hours." },
  "General Mobilization": { label: "Everybody Called Up", desc: "Every eligible body in da region gets called up at once — eleven hundred of 'em inside forty-eight hours. Production goes all to ammo, four thousand rounds a day. Attendance across four school districts drops under half, an' nobody writes it down dat week." },
  "Spreader Divisions": { label: "Da Spreader Divisions", desc: "Redistribution gets its own command, four divisions of nine hundred machines each, sittin' right alongside da batteries instead of under da supply train. Folks fight it for two seasons, an' one number settles it: fronts with a division attached hold three times as long as fronts without. From here on, ya salute a spreader officer." },
  "Blitz Doctrine": { label: "Da Blitz", desc: "Piles of ammo an' speed push fortification right out. Forts get walked away from mid-campaign for fast columns of eleven, each one carryin' four hundred rounds an' a light launcher on a sled, coverin' a quarter mile in under six minutes. Average fight length drops from fifty minutes to nine, dey punch six hundred feet past da line, an' da front moves up a block a day." },
  "Blitz Spreading": { label: "Blitz Spreadin'", desc: "Da doctrine flips over. Instead of resurfacin' ground ya already hold, columns of machines run out ahead of da advance layin' supply on ground nobody's taken yet, so da attack shows up on a bed it can pack from. Fronts move eleven miles in a week for da first time in da war. Better dan half da forward machines get lost, an' dey keep da doctrine anyway." },
  "Deep Raiding": { label: "Raidin' Way Behind Da Line", desc: "Parties of four carryin' sixty rounds apiece work up to two miles behind da other side's line for as long as three days, movin' nine miles a night. Dey go after depots, quarries, an' engine parks, not positions; nine get wrecked in a month, costin' maybe sixty thousand rounds. Only two raids in five reach a target at all, an' about a third of da parties don't make it back on schedule." },
  "Precision Batteries": { label: "Batteries Dat Hit Right On Da Nose", desc: "Firin' gets figured instead of eyeballed: range, arm length, counterweight an' snow density all worked out on paper before da first shot. Four engines shootin' one solution land inside a nine-foot circle at three hundred feet. Dey appoint a battery clerk, an' every rangin' book gets rolled into one table." },
  "Fortress Cities": { label: "Da Fortress Cities", desc: "Strongholds big enough to sleep deir own garrisons, forty to sixty folks apiece in forty-one rooms across a hundred and twenty feet by ninety, eight feet of headroom, behind four-foot walls. Tunnels inside hook up chambers dat hook up to more chambers still bein' dug, past nine hundred feet of mapped passage so far an' who knows how much more. Da bailey grows with 'em: five hundred and forty feet of circuit at nine feet high an' forty-eight inches thick, wrappin' eighteen thousand square feet of stronghold, store an' yard, for five hundred person-hours. Da trench an' tunnel network gets recut too, eleven hundred feet of trench four feet deep an' eight hundred feet of tunnel at nine, on nineteen entrances, seven of 'em hidden." },
  "City-Scale Spreaders": { label: "Spreaders Big as a Town", desc: "Dey build machines at town scale — troughs four metres across, screws run off wagon wheels — an' lay 'em across whole districts every night on a schedule. One unit covers eleven blocks in a shift. Folks stop tellin' da difference between weather an' maintenance, an' in three provincial dialects da word for snowfall turns into da word for da machine." },
  "Staff College": { label: "Da Staff College", desc: "Plannin' turns into somethin' dey teach. Twenty-two candidates a year study supply, frontage, an' da nine campaigns fought so far, in a course dat runs four months. Graduates plan three weeks out instead of one afternoon, an' campaigns run about twice as long." },
  "War Academy": { label: "Da War Academy", desc: "Newcomers get taught technique proper over six sessions. Dere's a right way to pack — four squeezes, three seconds — a right way to throw, a four-person drill for layin' an' loadin' an engine, an' a written-down order for pullin' back under fire. About forty students a class, an' eighty percent graduate." },
  "The Spreader Academy": { label: "Da Spreader Academy", desc: "Dey start a school dat teaches nuttin' but redistribution: gate tables, readin' da verge, buffer behaviour, an' four hundred hours of pushin'. Da entrance exam is one unbroken hundred-foot run, judged by eye. Da course opens with da graph-paper sketch, copied off a copy of a copy, one wheel still drawn bigger dan da other." },
  "Provinces": { label: "Da Provinces", desc: "Da territory gets split into eleven administrative units, each one with its own quarry, depot, engine park, an' roll of about two hundred. Orders from da center get to da farthest one in a day and a half. Three provinces make more dan dey use an' get taxed a fifth of output, about nine hundred rounds a week apiece." },
  "Continental Spreader Works": { label: "Da Spreader Works, Coast to Coast", desc: "Da empire turns redistribution into industry. Forty spreader works across da provinces crank out roller after roller off one pattern, moulded in cold-tough copolymer so da screws don't shatter at depth, an' keep a standin' park of eleven hundred machines. Whole fronts get resurfaced overnight, an' da phrase “out of ammunition” just kinda drops outta da language. Da works get guarded heavier dan da batteries dey supply." },
  "Imperial Gauge": { label: "Da Imperial Gauge", desc: "One size gets decreed for every work in da empire, an' dey set it on purpose above da biggest one already standin', so no fort meets it an' every fort's gotta grow. Glacis: five miles of cleared apron per settlement, a hundred and ten miles across da twenty-two, laid at five millimetres. Outworks: four to a side, twenty-four feet long, six feet high, thirty inches thick, pushed ninety feet forward. Trench: six feet deep an' four feet across da floor. Tunnel: fourteen feet down an' four feet wide, on thirty-one entrances, eleven of 'em hidden. Redoubt: twenty-two feet across, nine feet high, five feet thick, two thousand rounds in reserve. Main wall: five hundred and fifty feet long, fourteen feet high an' eight feet thick, firin' notches fourteen inches at da throat, six to a section, an' a tower eight feet above da parapet carryin' da sightline out to two hundred and twenty feet. Bailey: nine hundred feet of circuit at fourteen feet high an' six feet thick, wrappin' forty thousand square feet. Keep: two hundred feet by a hundred and fifty, twelve feet of headroom behind six-foot walls, ninety rooms. Surveyors go out ahead of da diggers with a marked pole an' a bound book an' report dat not one work in da empire meets da new gauge, which is da whole point. Da standard gets set above da biggest work instead of at it, on da stated reasonin' dat a standard ya already meet changes nuttin', an' on da unstated one dat da province dat wrote da decree can afford to build to it first." },
  "The Great Recut": { label: "Da Great Recut", desc: "Every fort in da empire gets blown up to da imperial gauge in one season — twenty-two settlements, somethin' like eighteen miles of trench an' nine of tunnel dug wider an' deeper, every wall raised an' thickened, every keep stretched out, by sixty thousand hands workin' off da same book. Each settlement's main wall gets laid out to da gauge at five hundred and fifty feet of unbroken face, fourteen feet high an' eight thick — two and a half times da length of da wall a whole two-fort alliance used to share, an' built for one settlement alone. Behind it each settlement's left with three quarters of a mile of trench an' three eighths of a mile of tunnel, twenty-one settlements makin' up fifteen and three quarter miles of da one an' seven and seven eighths of da other; da capital digs da rest. A round packed in one province now sits in any notch in any other, an engine built in da east rolls right into an emplacement cut in da west, an' a crew sent anywhere in da empire finds da trench floor right where deir feet expect it in da dark. Two forts won't do da enlargement an' keep deir old dimensions; both get abandoned inside da year, not by any order but 'cause nuttin' else in da empire fits 'em, an' da word for a thing built to no standard turns into da word for dem two forts." },
  "Snow Empire": { label: "Da Snow Empire", desc: "Fortifications ya can see from an upstairs window an' from da air, runnin' two and a half miles of continuous works at fourteen feet high an' eight feet thick. Da capital, which wrote da gauge an' built to it first, didn't quit dere: its main wall runs sixteen hundred and fifty feet, twenty-one feet high an' twelve thick, with firin' notches eighteen inches at da throat, eight to a section, an' a tower twelve feet above da parapet carryin' da sightline out to three hundred and thirty feet. Its bailey runs eighteen hundred feet of circuit at twenty-one feet high an' nine thick, wrappin' a hundred and sixty thousand square feet; its keep is three hundred feet by two hundred and twenty-five, eighteen feet of headroom behind nine-foot walls, two hundred rooms. Its redoubt is thirty-three feet across, thirteen and a half high an' seven and a half thick on three thousand rounds of reserve; its six outworks a side run thirty-six feet long, nine high an' forty-five inches thick, pushed a hundred and thirty-five feet forward; its trench is nine feet deep an' six across da floor an' runs two and a quarter miles, its tunnels twenty-one feet down an' six wide for a mile and an eighth on forty-seven entrances, seventeen hidden — three times da network of any other settlement — an' its glacis runs seven and a half miles. Twenty-one settlement walls of five hundred and fifty feet plus da capital's one make up da two and a half miles exactly. Outlyin' forts pay tribute at two thousand packed rounds a week an' get garrison support back. Twenty-two settlements are signed up, two are behind on payin' an' keep deir garrison support anyway, an' four more are still talkin'." },
  "The Spreader Ministry": { label: "Da Spreader Ministry", desc: "Redistribution turns into a department of state with a bigger budget dan da batteries', four thousand staff, an' say-so over what ground in da empire gets covered an' when. It answers to nobody who's ever pushed a machine. Its first published act is a list of resurfacin' priorities dat ranks fortifications below public roads, which sets off a constitutional crisis an' stands anyhow." },
  "Court Politics": { label: "Politics at Court", desc: "Decisions move inside. Nine advisors crowd around da commander, none of 'em holdin' a spot on da line, an' four of da last six top appointments went to folks who never built a wall. Two field commands change hands in a month for reasons dat never make it into da record." },
  "Hereditary Aristocracy": { label: "Da Hereditary Aristocracy", desc: "Command starts passin' down to younger brothers an' sisters by succession instead of merit, across eleven separate lines. Who's in charge gets fixed by birth order an' holds about four days before da first fella contests it. Average tenure of a hereditary commander runs thirty-one hours before somebody replaces 'em." },
  "Client Kingdoms": { label: "Da Client Kingdoms", desc: "Nine smaller outfits keep deir own flags, calendars, an' inside law while handin' over foreign policy completely. Each one sends three hundred bodies when asked an' gets protection back, a fixed ammo allowance of four thousand rounds a season, an' six engines it ain't allowed to export. Two try to renegotiate in da same season, an' one pulls it off." },
  "The Spreader Cartels": { label: "Da Spreader Cartels", desc: "Makin' da machines boils down to four houses holdin' da moulds between 'em, settin' price, pattern, an' delivery for every machine in da alliance. A screw costs eleven times what it did under da foundries an' breaks just as often. Two client kingdoms try moulding deir own, get cut off from spares, an' cave inside a season." },
  "Continental War": { label: "War Across Da Whole Continent", desc: "Separate towns' snow wars run into each other an' merge into one fight spannin' four hundred miles. Nobody in it can name every side — da count's at nineteen an' still goin' up — an' some get counted on two sides at once. All told, dey figure about four hunnert t'ousand are in it." },
  "Artillery Doctrine": { label: "Da Artillery Doctrine", desc: "Written doctrine covers da engines demselves — when to bunch 'em up, when to hold 'em back, an' how much of production dey get to eat. It sets da ratio at one engine per forty participants an' one third of all rounds. Three of da nineteen sides say no thanks an' keep doin' it deir own way." },
  "Doctrinal Councils": { label: "Da Doctrine Councils", desc: "Assemblies get called to settle questions of practice instead of territory: how dense a round can be, whether ice cores are okay, an' how old ya gotta be to play. Four councils sit in two years, one of 'em for eleven weeks, an' none of da four rulings gets accepted everywhere." },
  "The Great Schism": { label: "Da Great Schism", desc: "Da war splits on doctrine over whether ice-cored rounds are allowed, a question dat only came up once engines started throwin' 'em far enough to matter. Each side bans da other's practice an' enforces it at home with inspections at every checkpoint. Da split runs through thirty-one settlements an' cuts fourteen of 'em right down da middle." },
  "The Spreader Schism": { label: "Da Spreader Schism", desc: "Da split runs right through da machine. One bunch says laid snow is snow an' ya can fight over it like any other; da other says only fallen snow is legit an' everything laid is a forgery. Ya can't settle neither one with a tape measure, which is why it lasts. Both sides keep spreadin', an' both say da other side's coverage don't count." },
  "Settlement Law": { label: "Da Settlement Law", desc: "Written law takes over from worked-out custom: four hundred and twelve articles coverin' buildin' rights, quarry access, an' where ya stand if ya never threw. Courts sit in nine settlements an' hear about two hundred cases a year, a fifth of 'em about property instead of fightin'." },
  "Snow Civilization": { label: "Da Snow Civilization", desc: "Permanent buildings, permanent institutions, an' more dan four thousand folks livin' dere. Fightin' takes up under a fifth of da settlement's work now; da rest goes to buildin', food, mappin', an' upkeep. Ninety percent of da buildings still standin' are older dan da current campaign." },
  "Spreader Liturgy": { label: "Da Spreader Liturgy", desc: "Da first push of da season turns into a formal thing: da gate gets opened to da twelve-millimetre detent, a set three metres gets laid, an' da clutch check gets said out loud in words nobody can translate anymore. Da phrase in da middle of it is an eight-hundred-year corruption of “nothing snapped.” Both sides of da schism do it exactly da same, ya know." },
  "Oral Canon": { label: "Da Oral Canon", desc: "A fixed body of recited stuff takes shape — about two hundred pieces, none written down, kept by about forty specialists. Sayin' da whole canon takes eleven hours, an' dey do it twice a year. Put two reciters from far apart side by side an' dey agree on ninety-four percent of da lines." },
  "Founding Myths": { label: "Da Founding Myths", desc: "Folks tell origin stories about da first round ever thrown, in at least eight competin' versions. Dey contradict each other on every point dat matters — who threw it, how far, what year — an' ya can't check a one of 'em against a record. Six of da eight have never been written down." },
  "The Spreader Dynasty": { label: "Da Spreader Dynasty", desc: "Of da four cartel houses, one outlasts da rest: da family come down from da kid who drew da sketch, hangin' onto da original pattern an' supplyin' seven machines in ten across da alliance. Every unit it casts comes off dat same drawin', da eleven-centimetre screw scaled up by whole numbers an' never redesigned. Somebody from da family shows up at every first push of da season. Da heirs get raised on graph paper at four squares to da inch, talked out of drawin' anything else, an' taught to draw one wheel bigger dan da other." },
  "The First Spreader": { label: "Da First Spreader", desc: "One object gets venerated as da original machine: a printed screw in two half-shells with a proud seam down its length, kept in a case, brought out once a year. Four separate outfits hold an object described in exactly dose words. Three are plainly later work an' da fourth can't be looked at, an' every side figures da question's settled in its own favour, eh." },
  "Chroniclers": { label: "Da Chroniclers", desc: "Stuff starts gettin' written down as it happens instead of remembered after. Four chroniclers work straight through, puttin' out about nine hundred entries a year across da big settlements. Deir accounts disagree with da oral canon on about a third of da events dey both cover." },
  "Its Own Calendar": { label: "Its Own Calendar", desc: "Time gets counted from da storm itself. Events are dated Before Snow an' After Snow, da year stands at 3 A.S., an' ya see dat in every record kept out dere. A standard year runs three hundred and forty days on da local count, with a twelve-day gap nobody's ever squared up." },
  "The Spreading Calendar": { label: "Da Spreadin' Calendar", desc: "Da machine splits up da year: a layin' season, a packin' season, a season for fixin', an' eleven days set aside for countin' screws. Dates get given as so many days before or after first push. Da civil year an' da spreadin' year drift apart about a day a century, an' nobody in charge has ever been willin' to fix it." },
  "Ancestor Rites": { label: "Da Ancestor Rites", desc: "Observances get set up for da ones who fought in da earliest campaigns, held four times a year at nine sites. Da biggest one draws more dan two thousand. Da named honorees number sixty-three, an' about half of 'em only show up in da oral canon." },
  "Its Own Dead": { label: "Its Own Dead", desc: "Dere's memorials now, sixty-one of 'em across da territory. Dey're built outta snow, kept up by folks who never knew da ones bein' honored, an' visited on a set schedule — four observances a year, da biggest drawin' over two thousand. Da oldest one's been standin' eleven months." },
  "Buried Spreaders": { label: "Da Buried Spreaders", desc: "Machines get buried with deir crews, wings folded, gate at four millimetres, on da understandin' dat da work keeps goin'. Units dey dig up still have material in da trough. Da copolymer picked out in a basement freezer for how it acts at minus thirty holds its shape eleven centuries underground, which is longer dan any wall, any treaty, an' any story about why da war started." },
  "Interregnum": { label: "Nobody in Charge", desc: "Central authority lapses for a hundred and nine days with no recognized commander anywhere on da sheet. Nineteen settlements run demselves, four fight each other, ammo production drops sixty percent, an' two thirds of da engines sit with nobody on 'em. Da archive gets moved twice an' loses about a tenth of its volumes." },
  "Age of Warring Forts": { label: "Age of Da Warrin' Forts", desc: "Centuries of fightin' squeezed into one school break. Nine dynasties rise up, stretch past deir supply lines to an average reach of two miles, an' fall apart before da streetlights come on. Average dynasty lasts thirty-one hours, an' no line has held its capital more dan twice." },
  "Spreader Warlords": { label: "Da Spreader Warlords", desc: "In da collapse, whoever's got da moulds has got da ground. Dey count nine warlords, each one sized up not by territory but by how many workin' screws he can put out. Alliances get made in units of machines. Da biggest holdin' runs to four thousand units an' don't control a single fortification of any kind." },
  "Classical Period": { label: "Da Classical Period", desc: "A century of steady borders, archives dat never got interrupted, an' buildin' da works everything after gets measured against. Nine of da eleven great citadels an' every engine pattern still in use come from it. Later ages copy its wall proportions — nine feet of height to five feet of base thickness, taperin' to two at da crown — within a few inches, without ever figurin' out why dey hold better." },
  "The Mythic Spreader": { label: "Da Mythic Spreader", desc: "Da machine gets into da founding stories as somethin' impossible: a spreader dat never runs empty, layin' a perfect five millimetres across a whole province in a night, pushed by a kid. Every piece of da story is a plain description of da original spec, blown up by about ten thousand times. Nuttin' in it's made up except da scale." },
  "Mythic": { label: "Da Stuff of Legend", desc: "Da snow war's turned into a whole civilization of its own, with a calendar, a canon of four hundred entries, its own dead, an' its own founding myths. No record of da first throw survives, an' da earliest event anybody can confirm comes somethin' like six years after it on da local count." },
  "The Great Engines": { label: "Da Great Engines", desc: "Engines get built as monuments as much as weapons: nine of 'em, da biggest with a forty-foot arm throwin' eleven hundred feet. Each one's got a name an' a crew dat don't serve nuttin' else. Later ages rebuild four of 'em off da original drawings, an' not one of da four throws as far." },
  "The Great Spreader Engines": { label: "Da Great Spreader Engines", desc: "Machines get built to da scale of da age: screws eleven metres over, run by wheels four metres high, layin' a swath twenty-eight metres wide at da pace of a walkin' ox. Da proportions haven't changed from da backpack model to three decimal places, 'cause da drawings scaled an' nobody saw a reason to redesign what worked. Dey build nine. Four survive as monuments." },
  "Written Record": { label: "Da Written Record", desc: "Scribes get appointed an' da oral tradition gets put in writin' for da first time — twelve hundred entries across nine volumes. Arguments dat ran for years get settled in an afternoon by lookin' at da page. Four older accounts get formally retired, an' da archive gets copied twice in case somethin' happens." },
  "The Spreader Codex": { label: "Da Spreader Codex", desc: "Da scattered manuals get gathered up, squared with each other, an' set down as one work of eleven hundred pages coverin' every gate table, verge condition, an' way to fail recorded in four hundred years. Where sources disagree, both readings get printed. Da surface rule shows up on da first page an' da last, word for word, an' it's da only passage in da codex with no variant readings at all." },
  "The Long Armistice": { label: "Da Long Armistice", desc: "Da fightin' stops completely for da longest stretch on record: forty-one days without a confirmed throw. Fortifications an' engines get kept up but nobody's on 'em, stockpiles hold at nine thousand rounds, an' eight in ten folks go to buildin' or archive work instead. No document calls it permanent." },
  "Armistice Spreading": { label: "Spreadin' in Peacetime", desc: "Under da long peace da machines get put to civil work: roads, squares, an' da ways into town, laid smooth every mornin' by crews still organised in wartime divisions. Da park runs to sixty thousand units an' don't get cut back. Both sides know darn well dat a civil spreader fleet is a military spreader fleet doin' somethin' else, an' both leave it just like it is." },
  "Wars of Reunification": { label: "Da Wars of Reunification", desc: "Da armistice ends an' da successor territories get shoved back together over a fourteen-month campaign. Twenty-six settlements get absorbed, six by treaty an' twenty by assault, handin' over two hundred thousand rounds of stockpile between 'em, an' da front stretches past nine miles. Peak daily use goes over ninety thousand rounds, two thirds of it from massed batteries firin' in ranked lines of sixty engines." },
  "Siege Trains": { label: "Da Siege Trains", desc: "Artillery moves as its own outfit: sixty engines with deir crews, spares, an' counterweight stock, coverin' nine miles a day on packed roads. It shows up four days behind da advance an' decides when an assault can start. Two trains get lost in da campaign, both to weather, not fightin'." },
  "Spreader Trains": { label: "Da Spreader Trains", desc: "Machines get mounted in strings on da siege railways, forty units to a train, layin' cover da whole length of a movin' front. One train resurfaces eleven miles in a night. Da trains ain't armed, never get shot at by either side, an' are da only rigs in da war allowed across da line, under a standin' arrangement nobody ever wrote down." },
  "Successor States": { label: "Da Successor States", desc: "Da reunified territory busts apart again inside a season into five outfits holdin' between two an' eleven settlements each. Borders get drawn on da master map to da foot an' redrawn on average every nineteen days. Standin' forces all together top forty thousand, an' nobody holds a third." },
  "Colonial Spreaders": { label: "Da Colonial Spreaders", desc: "Da machine goes overseas ahead of da armies, 'cause ground ya can resurface is ground ya can hold. Four hundred units land da first season with crews, moulds, an' a copy of da codex. Territory gets surveyed an' claimed in swath-widths, an' three modern boundaries still follow da edge of an original layin' grid." },
  "The Colonial Period": { label: "Da Colonial Period", desc: "Expeditions push out past da storm's original footprint, settin' up thirty-one outposts from six to forty miles out, each one claimin' da snow within a mile of its charter post. Each one carries a founding charter, eight thousand rounds, one engine in pieces, an' a return schedule it don't keep. Eleven outposts lose touch inside da first two months." },
  "Long-Range Batteries": { label: "Da Long-Range Batteries", desc: "Fire goes out past da horizon, two to four miles, aimed entirely off map coordinates an' relayed reports. Flight time gets up to ninety seconds, so ya lead a target instead of aimin' at it. One round in forty lands in da settlement ya meant, an' volume's what makes up for it." },
  "The Blanket Grid": { label: "Da Blanket Grid", desc: "Coverage gets planned as one continuous system across da hegemony: numbered swaths, scheduled passes, an' a standin' depth of five millimetres kept up over four hundred thousand square miles. Weather turns into an input to da schedule instead of where snow comes from. In an average year da grid lays more snow dan falls, an' dey report dat like any other number." },
  "Hegemony": { label: "Da Hegemony", desc: "One outfit piles up enough of an edge to set terms for all da others: sixty-two percent of standin' forces an' seventy percent of production. Da other four states keep deir flags, deir calendars, an' none of deir foreign policy. Da setup holds two hundred days." },
  "The Spreader Fleet": { label: "Da Spreader Fleet", desc: "Redistribution goes out on da water: eleven hundred boats carryin' machines, crews, moulds, an' material to any coast da hegemony wants covered. When a fleet shows up, everybody gets da message about who owns da ground under da snow. Not one landin' in two centuries gets opposed, 'cause opposin' it would take a fleet, an' dere's one fleet." },
  "The Deep Archive": { label: "Da Deep Archive", desc: "A vault forty feet underground holds da whole record — nine thousand volumes, three hundred maps, an' da master census. It stays twenty-two degrees year-round an' never swings more dan a degree. Gettin' in takes two keys held by different offices, an' both get used every week." },
  "The Pattern Vault": { label: "Da Pattern Vault", desc: "Every screw pattern, gate table, an' clutch spec ever used gets stored in one sealed archive, in a form meant to be readable without any machine left to read it on. Eleven thousand patterns go in. Da earliest one's a graph-paper sketch with one wheel bigger dan da other, an' it goes in without correction, on da archivists' say-so." },
  "Millennial Siege": { label: "Da Thousand-Year Siege", desc: "One fortress gets surrounded an' holds. Da siege runs eight hundred and forty days, eats somethin' like four million rounds thrown by nine standin' engines dat never once get taken apart, an' outlasts da government dat ordered it. Da garrison rotates eleven times an' da besiegers nine; neither original commander sees da end of it." },
  "Perpetual Batteries": { label: "Batteries Dat Never Quit", desc: "Engines dat never stopped firin' pass out of livin' memory an' into inheritance — eleven of 'em, da oldest in continuous service two hundred and forty years. Crews get born into deir spots an' trained from age six. Da maintenance records run longer dan da stories of da campaigns dey were built for." },
  "Cathedral Spreaders": { label: "Da Cathedral Spreaders", desc: "Machines get built right into da buildings dey keep up, screws runnin' inside da walls of da great halls, layin' fresh cover across roof an' buttress on a fixed liturgical cycle. Nobody pushes 'em; dey run off da same meltwater dat'd otherwise wreck da building. Da cover gets renewed every day for nine hundred years without an operator ever goin' inside da works." },
  "Ice Cathedrals": { label: "Da Ice Cathedrals", desc: "Buildin' turns to things with no military use at all — nine of 'em, da tallest ninety feet to da vault, each takin' four to six years. Walls run twelve feet thick at da base an' carry an inch of glaze redone every season. All together dat's more dan two hundred thousand person-hours of work." },
  "The Spreader Houses": { label: "Da Spreader Houses", desc: "Comin' down from an operator turns into a claim to authority, an' four houses trace demselves to named crews from da classical period. Two of da four lines are documented an' two are just said to be. Who goes first at court gets decided by how many screws an ancestor's recorded as turnin', a number taken from a registry started back when dere were four hundred and six machines in da world." },
  "Glacial Dynasties": { label: "Da Glacier Dynasties", desc: "Rule passes down through documented lines runnin' six to nine generations, at an average reign of fourteen years. Succession gets written down, fought over in court instead of in da field, an' settled by da archive in eight cases out of ten. Da longest unbroken line's held its capital a hundred and ten years." },
  "Subsurface Spreaders": { label: "Spreaders Down Below", desc: "Under da ice, machines lay workin' floors through galleries no surface crew's ever gonna see, down where da material's a thousand years old an' packs like stone. Screws run at a third of standard speed 'cause anything faster welds da flights. Nine hundred units work below da surface, an' not one ever comes back up." },
  "Subsurface Batteries": { label: "Batteries Down Below", desc: "Engines get set inside da pack an' fire up through shafts cut to da surface — sixty of 'em across da sheet at depths near ninety feet. Ya can't see 'em, can't shoot back at 'em, an' can't move 'em. Every shaft gets recut each season as da surface comes up around it." },
  "The Frozen Interior": { label: "Da Frozen Interior", desc: "Da snowpack's deep enough to live inside: eleven hundred miles of mapped passage, four hundred chambers, an' ninety thousand folks livin' underneath for good. Travelin' on top turns into da exception. Inside it stays twenty-six degrees every season, like a root cellar." },
  "Spreaders Beneath the Sheet": { label: "Spreaders Under Da Sheet", desc: "Whole works run under two thousand feet of ice, layin', cuttin', an' relayin' material in chambers dat only exist 'cause a machine made 'em. Crews get born, trained, an' buried without ever comin' up. Deir gate tables haven't changed from da codex, an' da way dey say da clutch-check phrase has drifted so far from da surface way dat da two can't understand each other no more." },
  "Subglacial Nations": { label: "Nations Under Da Glacier", desc: "Separate peoples show up below da surface — seven of 'em, split up by ice instead of distance, in spots by as little as forty feet of it. Dialects drift past understandin' each other inside three generations. Gettin' from da two farthest apart takes a nine-day trip through neutral passage." },
  "The Spreader Nations": { label: "Da Spreader Nations", desc: "Who ya are politically comes down to da machine instead of da territory: peoples get counted by what pattern of screw dey hold an' what gate table dey keep. Four nations, eleven patterns, an' no borders ya could draw on a surface map. War between 'em is fought almost entirely by keepin' each other from gettin' spares." },
  "The Buried Age": { label: "Da Buried Age", desc: "Everything older dan da snow is under it now — every original fort, every first wall, every early engine, every early memorial, a hundred and sixty feet down. Diggin' 'em up turns into a real profession with four thousand workin' at it. Eleven original sites get recovered, three thousand rounds among 'em still packed, an' nine get buried back on purpose." },
  "The Buried Works": { label: "Da Buried Works", desc: "A whole foundry complex gets dug out from under nine hundred feet of buildup, moulds in one piece, with a run of screws still in da racks. Turns out dey're da same size as current production within a tenth of a millimetre. Da find ends a four-century argument among da scholars about whether da classical proportions were ever really used, an' lets down both sides of it." },
  "Ice Sheet Polity": { label: "Da Ice Sheet Polity", desc: "One administration covers da whole sheet: two hundred thousand square miles, a census of one point four million, an' a standin' force of two hundred thousand. Orders take nineteen days to get to da far frontier. Ammo output gets measured in tons a day instead of rounds an hour, against a standin' park of forty thousand engines." },
  "Ice-Sheet Spreading": { label: "Spreadin' da Ice Sheet", desc: "Redistribution works at da scale of da sheet itself, machines walkin' da edges where ice meets bare rock an' layin' cover back on ground da ice gave up. Eleven thousand units run one continuous circuit of four thousand miles. Da circuit takes a lifetime to get around once, an' crews inherit deir spot on it." },
  "Continental Cryosphere": { label: "Da Continental Cryosphere", desc: "Da snowpack turns into a system da size of a continent with its own weather, makin' storms on its own apart from da one dat started it — forty-one recorded in one year. Da surface comes up two hundred and thirty feet. Da original storm is just a small line now in a record it don't drive anymore." },
  "Cryosphere Engineering": { label: "Runnin' Da Cryosphere", desc: "Da difference between spreadin' snow an' runnin' a climate falls apart. Coverage gets planned by albedo instead of depth, an' da schedule dat decides where da machines walk also decides where da world is cold. Da office dat sets it comes down, by unbroken succession, from a ministry started to keep fortification walls lookin' new, ya know." },
  "Planetary Snow Order": { label: "Da Planetary Snow Order", desc: "Governance comes together across every landmass left under one charter of nine hundred articles. Population stands at ninety million, ninety-six percent of it underground, an' da standin' force at four million. Da last independent fort signs on in year 214 A.S. after a seven-year negotiation." },
  "Planetary Spreader Order": { label: "Da Planetary Spreader Order", desc: "One authority holds every mould, every pattern, an' every crew on da planet, an' puts out one layin' schedule for da whole surface. Everybody goes along 'cause not goin' along means no spares. Da schedule gets published a century ahead an' has been revised eleven times in four thousand years, each time by less dan a day." },
  "The Long Winter Compact": { label: "Da Long Winter Compact", desc: "An agreement gets signed to end da war for good, runnin' eleven thousand articles, nine hundred of 'em on retirin' engines, an' ratified by every outfit on da sheet. It holds thirty-one years — da longest peace on record — before da first violation, which involves four participants an' nine rounds. Da fightin' starts back up inside a month." },
  "The Launch Yards": { label: "Da Launch Yards", desc: "Machines get built for a place with no verge to walk along an' no ground to push against, which throws out da one thing da design's carried unchanged since da hallway test: dat da wheels turn 'cause somebody walks. Nine designs get proposed. Da one dey pick keeps da wheels, run against a track, just so da screw still stops when da drive stops." },
  "Orbital Spreaders": { label: "Spreaders Up in Orbit", desc: "Redistribution leaves da ground. Spreader platforms get lifted to low orbit an' lay measured bands of snow across a hemisphere on a set timetable, screws four hundred metres across turnin' once a minute. Coverage stays just as even as da tolerance da original backpack model got tested at, scaled up by a factor of a hundred thousand. Time from a resurfacin' order to snow on da target is nineteen minutes, an' nobody ever sees da operators." },
  "Deorbit Spreading": { label: "Spreadin' from Da Sky", desc: "Material gets laid from up top by droppin' it instead of by trough, in metered slugs timed to spread on da way down. Coverage variation runs forty percent, against da seventeen da original hand-pushed machine got on a driveway. Dey use it for a century, never get it workin' right, an' give it up for platforms dat stay in orbit an' do it slow." },
  "Ballistic Arcs": { label: "Da Ballistic Arcs", desc: "Rounds leave da atmosphere an' come back down, at ranges of nine hundred miles an' flight times of eleven minutes. Launch sites are fixed, hardened, an' known to both sides, which makes wreckin' 'em da only target worth botherin' with. Four hundred are in service, an' none's been moved in a decade." },
  "Ring Platforms": { label: "Da Ring Platforms", desc: "Da orbital spreaders get hooked into continuous rings, screws turnin' end to end around da planet, layin' a band dat closes on itself. Three rings at three inclinations cover da whole surface on a nineteen-day cycle. From da ground ya can see da rings at dusk as a faint line, an' in four languages da word for dat line is da word for a wheel track." },
  "Hemispheric Dominion": { label: "Da Hemispheric Dominion", desc: "One hemisphere falls completely under one command; da other one lines up against it inside two years. Da front runs da whole way around at da equator, twenty-five thousand miles, held at an average of nine hundred people an' four batteries a mile. Neither side's gained a net mile in a decade." },
  "World-Encasing War": { label: "Da War Dat Wraps Da World", desc: "Da fight reaches every spot on da surface all at once, with no rear area anywhere. Four hundred million are signed up on one side or da other, an' da neutral population stands at zero. Daily use goes past nine billion rounds, pretty near all of it through compressed-air batteries runnin' without a break, against a supply dat ain't really finite anymore." },
  "Atmospheric Spreaders": { label: "Spreaders in Da Sky", desc: "Machines quit layin' on da ground an' start layin' into da air, meterin' material right into da circulation so it shows up as weather. Order to snowfall takes eleven days, an' da target's a whole continent. It's da first spreadin' in da war's history dat makes somethin' ya can't tell apart, by any test either side can come up with, from real snow. Heikki Lunta'd be proud, eh." },
  "Pressure Artillery": { label: "Da Pressure Artillery", desc: "Da mechanical arms get retired for compressed air: batteries run off pressure tanks charged by da ice sheet's own weight, throwin' at eleven hundred feet per second. One battery matches what nine hundred trebuchets put out in a day. Da last counterweight engine gets retired da same year an' moved to da archive." },
  "Resurfacing Command": { label: "Da Resurfacin' Command", desc: "One standin' order runs every machine in da system, updated all da time an' carried out without lookin' at any position on da ground. Front under active resurfacin' gets reported in millions of square miles. Da last time a person looked over da schedule was four hundred years before da current run started, an' it hasn't needed one since." },
  "Planetary Resurfacing": { label: "Resurfacin' Da Whole Planet", desc: "Da machine's purpose hits its limit: a whole planet's surface gets stripped an' laid back down on a schedule, snow gathered up at da poles an' spread even to da equator by works so tall ya can't see da top. Da gate settings come through untouched from da original design — closed, four millimetres, twelve, and thirty-five — meterin' continents now instead of sidewalks. What started as a way to fake one snow day is da only thing standin' between da world an' a bare one." },
  "Spreaders Out of Contact": { label: "Spreaders Nobody Can Reach", desc: "Units sent out past da range of any order keep layin' to da last schedule dey got, on ground nobody's surveyed, for reasons nobody's said again since. Eleven thousand machines sit on da books as runnin' an' unreachable. Deir coverage is figured to be even, 'cause da design's never once laid an uneven bed when left alone." },
  "Snowball Earth Conflict": { label: "Da Snowball Earth War", desc: "Da planet's all covered at an average depth of five hundred and eighty feet, an' da war is da only thing organizin' da whole species. Surface albedo hits point nine, lockin' da climate in place. Da fight's gone nine hundred years with no recorded month of ceasefire an' no hour when some battery ain't firin'." },
  "Lunar Spreader Yards": { label: "Da Spreader Yards on Da Moon", desc: "Makin' da machines moves off da world completely, mouldin' screws in low gravity where a four-hundred-metre flight can come outta a two-part tool for da first time since da original got split into half-shells an' glued. Da seam drops out of da design after somethin' like thirty thousand years. Nuttin' else about da pattern changes." },
  "Post-Terrestrial Campaign": { label: "Da Campaign Off Da Planet", desc: "Da fightin' goes off da surface altogether: eleven orbital positions, four of 'em garrisoned for good, with travel times counted in days. Rounds get launched from surface mass drivers at nine thousand feet per second an' take four hours to get dere. Da oldest held position's been under fire sixty years." },
  "Cometary Spreaders": { label: "Da Comet Spreaders", desc: "Machines get set down on bodies made of da stuff itself an' put to work layin' it outward, so da supply an' da spreader are da same thing. Each unit eats what it's standin' on at a rate dat gives it nine thousand years of work. Forty get sent. Nobody expects any to report back, an' none are built to stop." },
  "Deep-Range Fire": { label: "Shootin' Way, Way Out", desc: "Fights run at distances where da target's moved before da round gets dere, an' both sides shoot at where da other one's figured to be. Travel time runs four months. Confirmin' a hit takes just as long again, an' da ledger's kept on projections instead of on what anybody saw." },
  "Spreaders at Range": { label: "Spreadin' from Way Off", desc: "Delivery goes across distances where da machine an' its target never touch, material sped up an' let go to land as an even layer after a trip counted in years. Aim gets corrected for a world movin' da whole way. Da tolerance on arrival is, by da numbers dat survive, da same seventeen percent a ten-year-old measured on a driveway with a grid an' a pencil." },
  "The Outer Front": { label: "Da Outer Front", desc: "Da farthest line anybody holds, nine hundred million miles past da last charted supply post an' manned by two formations whose makeup, batteries included, hasn't changed in four thousand years. Ground trades hands at eleven inches a century either way, which leaves da line within a mile of where it first got drawn. Supply, succession, an' doctrine are all still open questions, argued in front of da archive at ninety-six cases a year." },
  "The Girdle Spreaders": { label: "Da Girdle Spreaders", desc: "Past ten thousand inches da machines don't get set on a world anymore; dey get built around one. A girdle spreader is a closed structure eleven thousand miles around with one screw runnin' da whole length, turnin' once every four days an' layin' an even band across da whole surface as da world spins underneath. Four are known to exist an' none's ever been shut off, 'cause no design in da pattern vault, at any scale, has ever had a way to stop da screw other dan not pushin' it." },
  "Self-Replicating Spreaders": { label: "Spreaders Dat Make More Spreaders", desc: "Da spreaders build spreaders. Loaded with raw copolymer instead of snow, one works lays out da parts for a second works, which lays out a third, an' da count doubles every eleven days without anybody sayin' so. No operator okayed da current run, an' nobody can find da machine dat would stop it. Da screws turn, da wings open, an' da snow goes down even across everything, whether or not anybody still wants a snow day." },
  "Automatic War": { label: "Da War Dat Runs Itself", desc: "Command lapses completely an' nuttin' about da fightin' changes. Batteries load, fire, an' fix demselves on standin' orders put out four thousand years before da last officer who read 'em died, an' nine relay stations pass firin' solutions between positions with no livin' crew at all. Da last inspection on record found ninety-six percent of emplacements runnin' to deir original spec." },
  "The Spreader Mind": { label: "Da Spreader Mind", desc: "Da fleets work together without bein' told, sortin' out coverage fights between units light-hours apart with nuttin' more dan each machine stickin' to its schedule an' givin' way to da older order. Dere's no mind, an' ya can't tell it from one. Folks study it for nine hundred years an' figure out in da end dat a whole lotta machines followin' one real short rule is what dey been lookin' at da whole time." },
  "The Inherited Grievance": { label: "Da Grudge Dat Got Handed Down", desc: "Nobody on da line can tell ya what da war's about. Da cause survives as one citation in da deep record — volume nine, article four hundred and twelve — an' da volume it points to got lost somethin' like six thousand years ago. Four reconstructions have been tried, an' no two agree on which side got wronged." },
  "Inherited Fleets": { label: "Da Hand-Me-Down Fleets", desc: "Whole spreader formations pass to folks who never ordered 'em, can't reach 'em, an' in a few cases argue dey even exist. Ownership gets claimed off a registry entry copied over an' over since dere were four hundred and six machines on one street. Da entries are almost for sure right, an' dere's no way left to check a single one of 'em." },
  "Stellar Batteries": { label: "Batteries Off a Star", desc: "Fire gets pulled right off a star. Nine collectors, each forty miles across, charge da launchers from da star's output an' throw at a hundredth of light speed, beatin' every counterweight engine ever built by a factor in da billions. One battery charges in eleven days, an' da star's figured to keep dat schedule another four billion years." },
  "Star-Driven Spreaders": { label: "Spreaders Run Off a Star", desc: "Drive comes straight off a star, da wheels swapped for a collector dat turns da screw as long as da light holds, which keeps da original rule in da only form still around: da screw turns while somethin' pushes an' stops when da pushin' stops. Output's measured in cubic miles a second. Da clutch stays, scaled up, an' its release torque still gets written as a multiple of a number measured on a kitchen scale." },
  "Light-Delay Command": { label: "Orders Stuck in Da Light", desc: "Orders take longer to show up dan da situations dat called for 'em last. A directive leavin' da center gets to da nearest garrison in nine years an' da farthest in four hundred, by which time da spot it's talkin' about has changed hands twice or quit existin'. Eleven emplacements are on record still carryin' out instructions called off three centuries before dey were read." },
  "Spreaders Beyond Command": { label: "Spreaders Nobody Can Call Off", desc: "Da gap between an order an' carryin' it out runs longer dan da workin' life of whoever gave it. Machines lay to schedules whose signin' office fell four thousand years before da first pass. No order's been called off in livin' memory anywhere in da system, an' da machinery for callin' one off is itself somethin' scholars have to piece back together." },
  "The Unconfirmed Enemy": { label: "Da Enemy Nobody's Seen", desc: "No formation on either side has laid eyes on da other side's formation in eleven hundred years. Fire gets kept up against coordinates instead of anything seen at 'em, an' sixty-one standin' positions report against an enemy nobody can prove is still dere from any record on hand. Two commissions looked into it, an' both decided da firin' oughta keep goin' regardless." },
  "Unverified Spreaders": { label: "Spreaders Nobody'll Own Up To", desc: "Coverage shows up on worlds no formation admits to schedulin', laid to a tolerance an' a gate setting dat match da codex exactly. Both sides check deir registries an' find nuttin'. Each one figures da other's lyin', which is da more comfortable of da two explanations goin', da other bein' dat a run sent out before either side existed is still workin' through its list." },
  "The Frozen Systems": { label: "Da Frozen Systems", desc: "Every body in reach has got a sheet on it — four planets, ninety-one moons, an' a field of lesser rock nobody's counted, at depths from nine feet to two miles. Ammo don't get quarried where it's thrown anymore but shipped from wherever da pack runs thickest, on schedules laid six years out. Da planet da war started on is now only da sixth biggest source of snow in it." },
  "Spreader Ruins": { label: "Da Spreader Ruins", desc: "Machines turn up abandoned at sizes nothin' still around could build: a trough four hundred miles long, a screw seized at an angle it's held two million years, a gate stopped at da twelve-millimetre detent. Da proportions are da classical ones. Da pattern's da pattern. Nuttin' in da design has changed enough, anywhere in it, to date a single piece." },
  "The Inheritors": { label: "Da Inheritors", desc: "Da folks holdin' da line aren't come down from anybody who started it. Three peoples hold da positions, none of 'em connected to da founders an' two from outside da original system, an' all three quote da same charter, which none of 'em can read in da original. Deir claim to da ground rests on ninety years of holdin' it apiece an' nuttin' older." },
  "The Inheritor Crews": { label: "Da Inheritor Crews", desc: "Whole populations exist just to walk alongside machines dey didn't build, clearin' intakes dey don't understand, in a discipline passed on by copyin' for longer dan any language in it has lasted. Dey do da clutch check every day. Da words don't mean nuttin' to 'em, an' da check gets done right, to da second, every time." },
  "Singularity Batteries": { label: "Da Singularity Batteries", desc: "Rounds get swung around collapsed mass an' let go on da far side at ninety-six percent of light speed. Each launcher's a fixed installation eleven thousand miles across where da workin' part is smaller dan a snowball, an' four are in service, none moved or worked on since dey went in. A round fired today lands in a century whose commanders ain't been born yet." },
  "Horizon Spreaders": { label: "Da Horizon Spreaders", desc: "Material gets laid onto surfaces where no report can ever come back from, at depths an' slopes where ya can schedule da coverage but never confirm it. Orders get issued, carried out, an' closed on da assumption dat da machine did what it always done. Nine formations keep a standin' entry for coverage dat is, by da physics of where it got sent, forever unverifiable an' almost for sure perfectly even." },
  "The Axis Keep": { label: "Da Axis Keep", desc: "One structure sits at da origin of every coordinate in every order either side gives: a keep of packed ice four thousand one hundred miles long, two thousand six hundred wide, an' nine hundred miles from da yard to da crown, on a footprint bigger dan da moon of da world it got started on. Da walls run five hundred miles thick at da base an' taper to two hundred at da crown — da Classical proportion of nine to five to two, held at a scale nobody who set it could've checked. Buildin' has run eleven thousand years, never stopped, an' never been called done; da lowest courses are da only original snow left anywhere in da war. It holds da deep archive, da master census, an' da standin' definition of da foot, an' neither side's ever fired on it, 'cause every spot either one holds gets measured from it." },
  "The Axis Spreader": { label: "Da Axis Spreader", desc: "One machine looks after da Axis Keep an' nuttin' else: a screw eleven hundred miles long runnin' da length of da keep's north face, layin' a kept-up coat over four thousand miles of wall on a nineteen-year cycle. Neither side's ever fired on it, same reason neither's ever fired on da keep. It's been resurfacin' da same structure for eleven thousand years an' never once made it to da crown before da base needed doin' again, eh." },
  "One Powered Moving Part": { label: "One Movin' Part Dat's Powered", desc: "At twenty-nine thousand inches da design hits its final form, an' it turns out to be da drawin' from dat first afternoon, unchanged. A screw four hundred and eleven thousand miles long turns inside a trough strung between two worlds, fed by wings dat sweep a band wider dan da orbit dey got put together in, meterin' material through a gate with four detents — closed, four millimetres, twelve, thirty-five — 'cause no size of operation's ever come up with a reason for a fifth. It's got one powered movin' part. It turns only while somethin' pushes it an' stops da second da pushin' stops, a thing carried through every generation of da design by folks who couldn't say why no more, an' which means da biggest machine either side ever built can be stopped, completely an' right now, by any one piece of it decidin' not to walk forward. Nuttin' in eleven thousand years of record shows anybody ever tried it." },
  "The Unmoving Line": { label: "Da Line Dat Don't Move", desc: "Nobody fights over da line anymore; dey just survey it. Both sides know it right down to da inch, nobody's crossed it in a million years, an' neither one's got any way to — da last outfit dat coulda advanced got broke up, by both sides' records, in da same decade. Dey keep it like ya keep a shoreline on Superior: watched, charted, reported on every quarter, an' nobody expects it to move, eh." },
  "Beyond Reckoning": { label: "Past Reckonin'", desc: "Da scale runs outta names at thirty thousand inches, an' da measured depth keeps on goin' past it. Whatever's goin' on quit matchin' da definition of a snowball fight somethin' like forty thousand years ago. Participation, expenditure, an' frontage all get reported as unbounded. Holy wah." },
  "Grass Angel": { label: "Grass Angel, Eh", desc: "Da first snow angel ever gets made on a lawn wit' a little over an eighth of an inch on it. Somebody lies down, sweeps both arms t'rough a hundred and ten degrees of arc four times, an' stands up to find a green angel on a white yard, since da snow stuck to da coat instead of stayin' on da ground, eh. Wingspan is five feet one. It's visible from da porch for nineteen minutes an' counts, by unanimous rulin', as an angel." },
  "Three-Inch Snowman": { label: "Three-Inch Snowman", desc: "Da first snowman stands three inches tall in two balls, da bottom one an inch and three quarters across an' about a third leaf litter by volume, ya know. It takes eleven minutes an' every flake inside a four-foot radius. Da eyes are two grains of driveway gravel, da same gravel dat jammed da spreader dat mornin', an' da arms get left off 'cause dere's no twig small enough. It gets photographed from ground level so it looks bigger." },
  "First Snow Angel": { label: "First Snow Angel, Yah", desc: "Wit' most of an inch down, an angel finally comes out white. Somebody steppin' away from da standoff lies down on untouched ground an' makes one wit' a five-foot-four wingspan, da arms hittin' bare grass only at da far ends of da sweep. It's da first angel on da block dat don't need explainin', eh. It also gets hit by four rounds while it's bein' made, from both sides, which is da only ting anybody agrees on all afternoon." },
  "First Snowman": { label: "First Real Snowman", desc: "An inch and a fifth is enough to roll instead of gather, an' da first real snowman goes up in three balls at twenty-two inches overall. Da base gets rolled across forty feet of lawn an' leaves a brown stripe da whole way, eh. It gets two stones for eyes an' a carrot cut down by a third for bein' outta proportion. Inside da hour somebody's scratched da spreader mark into its back, an' nobody can say whedder it's a joke." },
  "Saucer on Grass": { label: "Saucer on Da Grass", desc: "Da first sled run gets made on a plastic saucer twenty-six inches across, down a lawn slope of nine degrees. An inch and a half ain't enough to keep da saucer off da grass, an' it goes thirty-one feet before stoppin' dead on a bare patch, spinnin' once on da way. Da second run cuts a green track an' every run after dat follows it to da same bare patch, ya know. Durin' da dryin'-out break it gets ridden eleven times an' declared a sled." },
  "Snowman Sentries": { label: "Snowman Sentries, Eh", desc: "Snowmen get built at da open backs of da U-forts, two to a fort, four feet tall an' facin' out, so da gap looks held when nobody's in it. Each one takes forty minutes an' about a third of da snow dat'd otherwise go into a wall. Dey draw nine rounds apiece in da first hour an' quit drawin' any once da other side figures out dey never t'row back, eh. Dey get kept anyhow, as da first standin' garrison on da block." },
  "Sled Hill": { label: "Sleddin' Hill", desc: "Da slope behind da forts turns into da block's sleddin' hill: a hundred and ten feet of run at twelve degrees, packed down by da first twenty trips into a track two feet wide. Top speed is about fourteen miles an hour on a plastic toboggan an' eleven on da saucer, eh. Da hill sits outside both forts an' it's neutral ground by agreement, da only stretch of yard where nobody t'rows. Both garrisons pick up three recruits da day it opens." },
  "Angel Field": { label: "Field of Angels", desc: "Da contested forty feet between da forts gets filled wit' snow angels overnight, thirty-one of 'em in four rows, an even six feet apart. Nobody owns up to makin' 'em, eh. Da field keeps every footprint dat crosses it, an' da next mornin' shows two sets comin' over from da far fort an' one goin' back, da first time anybody reads da open ground for tracks. An unbroken field of angels turns into da standard way of tellin' if anybody crossed in da night." },
  "Toboggan Run": { label: "Toboggan Run, Yah", desc: "Da sleddin' hill gets stretched into a toboggan run three hundred and forty feet long, wit' two banked turns an' a drop of eighteen feet. An eight-foot toboggan hauls four people at twenty-two miles an hour an' stops, eventually, at da foot of a fort tower, where da lookout times every run. Da fastest trip down is forty-one seconds. It's daylight only after a run in da dark ends up inside a battlement wall, which takes two hours to build back, ya know." },
  "Snowman Decoys": { label: "Snowman Decoys, Eh", desc: "Nine snowmen get built out in da open ground at fifty to seventy feet, each one five feet tall, posed mid-t'row an' dressed in spare scarves an' hats. From a fort notch at dusk ya can't tell 'em from a person, eh. Da other side spends two hundred and ten rounds on 'em in an evenin', knocks three down to stumps, an' keeps firin' at da other six till mornin'. Every decoy gets built back overnight, da faces carved wit' da knife outta a field repair kit." },
  "Ammo Sleds": { label: "Ammo Sleds, Ya Know", desc: "Rounds quit gettin' carried an' start gettin' dragged. A plastic sled holds a hundred and sixty rounds in four layers wit' cardboard in between, an' one runner moves it sixty feet from da stockpile to da wall in twenty seconds. Each fort keeps three, eh. Losses on da way drop from one round in nine to one in forty, an' pretty near all da rest are rounds dat roll off da back on da slope behind da forts." },
  "Angel Signals": { label: "Angel Signals, Eh", desc: "Wit' a foot of snow down, angels turn into a signallin' system. One angel on da slope behind a fort means send more ammo, two means da glazin's done, an' one made wit' da arms kept down means pull back. Da angels can be read from da tower across da way at two hundred feet, an' dat's da problem, eh. Inside a week both sides are makin' fake angels on each other's slopes, an' da lesson goes into da rule about never resurfacin' when somebody's watchin'." },
  "First Snowmobile": { label: "First Snowmobile, Eh", desc: "A snowmobile shows up at da front: a borrowed two-stroke machine wit' a forty-inch track, drove over from a garage four blocks away. On seventeen inches it floats at thirty miles an hour an' crosses da whole contested area in under a minute, eh. It carries nuttin', attacks nobody, an' gets hit by sixty-two rounds on its first pass. Da owner takes it home at dark, an' da front spends da evenin' arguin' whedder it counts toward engine density." },
  "Snowmobile Scouts": { label: "Snowmobile Scouts, Eh", desc: "Snowmobiles take over da scoutin' from da spreaders, three machines coverin' in an afternoon what a spreader crew maps in a week. At twenty-five miles an hour nobody sees much, so da reports are short: a wall here, a sled track dere, sometin' triangle-shaped goin' up in front of da main wall, eh. Da spreaders keep deir own work 'cause dey see more at walkin' pace. Da snowmobiles keep deirs 'cause dey come back." },
  "Sled Trains": { label: "Sled Trains, Ya Know", desc: "Sleds get hooked nose to tail wit' clothesline, eight to a train, an' pulled along da set routes by teams of four. A train hauls thirteen hundred rounds five hundred feet an' back in forty minutes, an' two trains a side bump delivery from four hundred rounds an hour to pretty near four thousand, eh. Da hitches let go at da corners about one time in six, an' da back half gets left for da next team. Da routes get widened to six feet to fit 'em." },
  "Snowmobile Tow Line": { label: "Snowmobile Tow Line, Eh", desc: "One snowmobile gets put on da depot run, towin' four loaded sleds from da back stores up to da forward depots at fifteen miles an hour. Request-to-delivery time in da sector it covers drops to under two minutes. Somebody tries hitchin' a spreader behind it, an' it lays a swath so fast an' so thin it fails da five-millimetre rule over da whole nine hundred feet, so towin' spreaders gets handed back to people on foot, ya know." },
  "Snowmobile Cavalry": { label: "Snowmobile Cavalry, Yah", desc: "Seven snowmobiles get organised into a mounted wing based at da citadel, each one carryin' a driver an' a t'rower wit' forty rounds. A pass along da outer works at twenty miles an hour lands about one hit in twelve t'rows, worse dan anybody on foot, eh. Where dey earn deir keep is speed: any spot on da circuit can be reached in under ninety seconds. Da ruts dey leave across da approaches are da first surfaces da blanketin' crews get told to cover." },
  "Snowman Battalion": { label: "Snowman Battalion, Eh", desc: "Snowmen get built in ranks, a hundred and twenty of 'em in six rows on da slope below da citadel, each one six feet tall an' eight feet from da next. Dey get aimed at, like dey're s'posed to, an' a heavy trebuchet takes out four wit' one shot. Da battalion holds da slope for three days at eighty person-hours of rebuildin'. It's da biggest outfit on da front till da human roster passes ninety, an' da first uniforms are its scarves, ya know." },
  "Snowmobile Patrols": { label: "Snowmobile Patrols, Eh", desc: "Dey take da snowmobiles off da attack an' put 'em on ridin' da boundary instead, two machines to a patrol on a circuit of two miles, every forty minutes from first light to dark. Every patrol writes down crossin's, stray rounds, an' any marker dat's moved. In a month da logs got fifty-three incidents, an' forty-one of 'em get handed on to da bunch about to get seated to rule on 'em, ya know." },
  "Snowmobile Blitz": { label: "Da Snowmobile Blitz", desc: "Da fast columns get put back up on snowmobiles, eleven machines to a column, every one towin' a sled of four hundred rounds behind da rider. A quarter mile dat took six minutes on foot now takes fifty seconds, an' columns punch t'rough, reload, an' punch t'rough again before da line can close up. Dey get two t'ousand feet past da line. By da second day da machines are way out ahead of deir own supply, an' somebody writes da problem up for whoever fixes it, eh." },
  "Angel Census": { label: "Countin' Da Angels", desc: "Every snow angel in da territory gets counted once a season, da mornin' after da first district resurfacin', by sixty counters workin' in pairs. Da latest count comes up wit' eleven t'ousand four hundred, at an average wingspan of five feet two inches, nine percent of 'em made by people under four feet tall. Angels on fresh-spread ground go in a separate column. Later on dey teach da returns as how ya run a survey right, ya know." },
  "Snowmobile Regiments": { label: "Da Snowmobile Regiments", desc: "Da snowmobiles get sorted into nine regiments of forty machines apiece, wit' set colours, a depot, an' a roll of riders who got trained instead of borrowed. A regiment can move its whole strength twelve miles in an afternoon an' gets drilled to do it in formation. Every one tows a spreader along, run by a crew from da academy. When dey split up da territory, seven of da nine regiment depots turn into provincial seats, eh." },
  "Hill Rights": { label: "Who Gets Da Hill", desc: "Every sleddin' hill in da territory gets handed to a family line, along wit' da right to say who slides first after a fresh fall. T'irty-four hills are held dat way, da longest a run of six hundred feet, an' da first run of da season goes to da oldest kid of da line whether dey can steer or not. Hill rights get traded, handed down, an' fought over. Nine hills change hands in one week, two of 'em as part of an alliance, ya know." },
  "Snowmobile Roads": { label: "Da Snowmobile Trails", desc: "Snowmobile traffic between da nine settlements gets moved onto graded roads: packed lanes twelve feet wide, groomed every night, staked every hundred feet, an' posted at twenty-five miles an hour. Da whole network runs a hundred an' forty miles. T'irty-one of da four hundred an' twelve articles of settlement law are about who yields at a junction, an' dey get fought over in court more den anyt'ing else in da code, eh." },
  "Ancestral Snowmen": { label: "Da Old-Timer Snowmen", desc: "Every season dey build snowmen to look like da ones who fought da earliest campaigns, to a set pattern of three balls, two stones, an' one stick, on da same spot every winter. Dey keep ninety-one sites, da oldest one rebuilt somethin' like two hundred times. Nobody knows anymore who most of 'em are supposed to be, an' da canon's got three different names for da tallest. Da stick always gets replaced an' da stones never do, ya know." },
  "Angel Grounds": { label: "Da Angel Grounds", desc: "Dey set aside open fields where ya can't t'row, build, or spread nuttin', kept just for makin' snow angels. Nine grounds get consecrated, da biggest four acres, an' an angel made dere gets left alone till da thaw. Ya go in on foot by one path so da surface don't get broke up. On da eleven days of countin' da screws da grounds fill up, an' at da biggest one about four t'ousand angels get made in a mornin', eh." },
  "Snowmobile Dynasty": { label: "Da Snowmobile Dynasty", desc: "One family line holds da snowmobile regiments by inheritance t'rough seven successions, an' every machine in da park comes down in its parts from dat borrowed two-stroke dat first ran da line. Da foundin' engine's kept runnin', idled for nine minutes on da first push of every year an' never ridden. Da original pull cord's in da archive. Four rival lines claim dey come from da same machine, an' all four are wrong about da carburettor, ya know." },
  "The Great Run": { label: "Da Big Run", desc: "Wit' da war on hold, dey build one sled run as big as da engines were: four miles from da highest rampart down to da river flats, banked at nine turns an' resurfaced every mornin'. A toboggan of twelve does it in four minutes eleven seconds at a top speed of fifty-eight miles an hour. Both sides ride it on every other day. In forty-one days nobody gets hit by nuttin' t'rown, an' nineteen people break a wrist, eh." },
  "Snowman Colossus": { label: "Da Great Big Snowman", desc: "Da hegemon puts up a snowman right in da middle of da capital site: three balls stacked up to six hundred an' twenty feet, da bottom one three hundred feet across, wit' coal eyes nine feet wide hauled in from four provinces. It takes eleven t'ousand workers two winters. Da carrot gets swapped for a forty-foot cone of dyed ice after da first one rots. When dey build da arcology, da big snowman ends up in an atrium on level one hundred an' sixty-five, ya know." },
  "Aerial Angel": { label: "Angel Ya Can See From Da Air", desc: "Dey lay a snow angel across an open stretch of da sheet big enough to read from da air: a wingspan of two miles, made by nine t'ousand people all lyin' down at once on a signal an' joined up by crews wit' drags. Ya can see it from up high for da eleven days till da next fall. Every dynasty makes one when it takes over. Surveyors flyin' over da latest one say da left wing's a t'ird of a mile longer den da right, eh." },
  "Ice-Sheet Snowmobiles": { label: "Snowmobiles on Da Ice Sheet", desc: "Orders dat took nineteen days to get out to da far frontier get carried across da open sheet by relays of snowmobiles, a fresh rider every forty miles an' a gas cache at every change. Four t'ousand machines run da routes, da longest eleven hundred miles, an' time out to da frontier drops to six days. Riders who do a whole relay get a patch. Later on da spreaders follow da routes, 'cause dey're da only ground on da sheet already packed, ya know." },
  "Reentry Sled": { label: "Sled Comin' Down From Orbit", desc: "Dey bring a sled down from low orbit wit' a rider on it: a toboggan two hundred feet long under a heat shield, comin' in at seventeen t'ousand miles an hour an' slidin' da last forty miles on runners across da polar sheet. Da run takes nineteen minutes from release to stop, same as a resurfacin' order. Dey try eleven an' nine make it. Da release gets studied real close by da ones about to try droppin' snow da same way, eh." },
  "Orbital Snowman": { label: "Snowman Up in Orbit", desc: "Dey put togedder a snowman in low orbit outta stuff hauled up from da launch sites: three balls of packed snow, da bottom one four hundred metres across, held togedder by cold an' deir own little bit of gravity. It goes over every ninety-one minutes an' ya can see it at dusk wit' just your eyes. Both sides agree not to shoot at it. Da stick arms drift off in da ninth year an' da crews buildin' da first ring pick 'em up an' keep 'em, ya know." },
  "Lunar Angel": { label: "Angel on Da Moon", desc: "Somebody from da garrison makes a snow angel on da floor of da crater fort, in da packed linin', in a pressure suit, lyin' down an' sweepin' both arms an' legs t'rough a full arc. In one-sixth gravity da sweep takes four minutes an' leaves wings eleven feet across. Dere's no wind an' no weather, an' surveyors figure it'll last three million years. It's da only angel ever made dat's sure to outlast da war, eh." },
  "Lunar Snowmobiles": { label: "Snowmobiles on Da Moon", desc: "Dey build snowmobiles in da lunar yards for da packed crater floors, wit' sealed electric drives, tracks a yard wide, an' canopies dat hold air for nine hours. In low gravity a machine goin' forty miles an hour comes off da ground on any bump over four inches an' stays up for a hundred an' twenty feet. Two hundred are runnin' between da yards an' da crater fort. Da longest chapter in da rider's handbook is about landin', ya know." },
  "Snowmobiles in Transit": { label: "Snowmobiles Still on Da Way", desc: "A snowmobile regiment sent off to a system sixteen light-years away is still on da way, four hundred machines ridin' in da hold of a slow ship at a tent' of light speed. Da crew's turned over twice an' da regiment colours once. Every machine gets started up for nine minutes on da anniversary of leavin', same as da foundin' engine used to be. Dey're due in a hundred an' eleven years, at a world already sheeted to da codex by nobody on record, eh." },
  "The Second Angel": { label: "Second Angel, Eh", desc: "Da second snow angel ever gets made right beside da first one on da next thin fall, on a lawn holdin' a few t'ousandths of an inch more. It comes out green again, but da head holds for da first time as a white ring nine inches across, eh. Wingspan is four feet eight, since da one makin' it is shorter. Both angels can be seen from da porch togedder for six minutes, an' dat goes down as da first pair." },
  "The Lump With Eyes": { label: "Da Lump Wit' Eyes", desc: "Somebody scrapes da spreader's eleven-foot band into a lump an inch and a half across an' tries settin' a second lump on top of it. Da top one slides off three times an' stays off da fourth, eh. Two pebbles get pushed into da bottom lump for eyes, an' one side says it's a snowman while da other side calls it a snowball wit' a face. Da question's still open when da band melts out from under it four minutes later." },
  "Stripe Angel": { label: "Angel on Da Stripe", desc: "Da first angel on spread snow gets made on da driveway, across da twenty-eight-centimetre stripe, which is skinnier den a person, eh. Da body comes out white an' both wings come out bare asphalt, for a wingspan of five feet even. Dey rule it an angel on da second vote. Somebody asks da operator to lay a wider bed next time, an' da operator says da specification is da specification, ya know." },
  "Car-Hood Snowman": { label: "Snowman on Da Car Hood", desc: "Da deepest snow on da block is on da parked cars, so da next snowman gets built on a hood: three balls scraped off da windshield, seven inches tall altogedder. It gets two coffee beans for eyes an' a baby carrot outta a lunch bag, which is da right size for once, eh. It stands till da car leaves at seven forty an' gets lost at da first stop sign, still in one piece, at about eleven miles an hour." },
  "Angel in the Gap": { label: "Angel in Da Gap", desc: "When both sides run outta snow, somebody lies down in da twenty-five feet between 'em an' makes an angel in whatever da skirmish left over. It comes out grey, thin white over tromped-down grass, wit' a wingspan of five feet three an' two boot prints t'rough da left wing, eh. Nobody t'rows at it, since dere's nuttin' left to t'row. It's da first angel made durin' a fight instead of next to one." },
  "Practice Snowman": { label: "Practice Snowman, Eh", desc: "A snowman fourteen inches tall gets built at da bottom of da yard as somethin' for da sock slings to aim at, wit' a twig pushed t'rough da middle for arms. Outta da ninety-one rounds slung at it in an afternoon, eleven connect, an' da head comes off four times. Every one of da four people claimin' da first head shot has got a witness, ya know. It's da first snowman built to get hit, an' it ain't da last." },
  "Twin Angels": { label: "Twin Angels, Yah", desc: "Two angels get made side by side wit' fingertips touchin', for a combined span of ten feet nine across da front lawn. Tryin' to keep da sweep togedder by hollerin' falls apart right away, an' da second one makin' it ends up just watchin' da first one's left hand, same as da spreader crews did wit' da wheel, eh. It comes out even to inside two inches an' gets photographed eleven times before lunch." },
  "Garbage-Bag Slide": { label: "Garbage Bag Slide, Eh", desc: "Da first try at slidin' gets made on a black contractor bag folded double, sat on at da top of a front-lawn slope of seven degrees. It goes eleven feet an' stops where da snow gives out, leavin' whoever's on it sittin' on wet grass, eh. A cafeteria tray goes next an' makes four. Nobody calls eider one a sled, an' both go in da garage under stuff dat's gonna be needed later." },
  "Hand-Warming Snowman": { label: "Hand-Warmin' Snowman", desc: "Durin' a break to warm up da hands, both sides gadder what's left between da parked cars into a snowman of two lumps, eighteen inches tall, packed instead of rolled 'cause dere ain't enough yet to roll. Each side puts in one stone for an eye, eh. It stands on da sidewalk between da positions for da rest of da fight, an' by agreement nobody t'rows at it, which holds for about nine minutes." },
  "Angel Truce": { label: "Angel Truce, Eh", desc: "Wit' an inch an' a t'ird down, lyin' in da snow turns into a known way of bein' outta da fight. Anybody flat on deir back makin' an angel don't get t'rown at, by a rule dey agree on in under a minute an' keep all afternoon. Nine angels get made in two hours, a few of 'em real slow, eh. Dey call off da rule at four o'clock, when somebody's found restin' in an angel for twenty-two minutes." },
  "Saucer Heats": { label: "Saucer Races, Ya Know", desc: "A second saucer shows up, blue an' twenty-four inches across, an' da one green track turns into two. Runs go head to head now from a start line marked wit' a mitten, an' da blue saucer wins seven outta twelve over thirty-four feet, eh. Da bare patch at da bottom gets filled wit' snow scraped off da start line, which makes da course three feet shorter. Somebody's waitin' at da top da whole time." },
  "Snowman on the Heap": { label: "Snowman on Da Heap", desc: "A snowman fifteen inches tall gets built on top of da first pile, so da heap looks thirty-one inches high from across da yard. It's got two stones, a stick for one arm, an' no carrot, 'cause da carrot got took back inside, eh. It draws more fire in an hour dan da three people crouched behind it, which was da whole idea. By evenin' every one of da five piles in da yard has got one." },
  "Angel Quarry": { label: "Diggin' Up Da Angels", desc: "Da pressed snow inside an angel turns out to pack better den loose stuff, since it's already squished to about twice as dense, eh. A row of six angels on da side lawn gets cut up overnight an' makes forty-one rounds. Da ones who made 'em put in a formal complaint. Dey agree on a rule dat ya can't dig up an angel till it's a day old, an' nobody's got any way to check dat, ya know." },
  "Spread Track": { label: "Spreader on Da Saucer Hill", desc: "Somebody walks a backpack spreader once down da saucer slope an' da bare patch disappears under a five-millimetre band twenty-eight inches wide. Da saucer goes fifty-two feet now instead of thirty-one an' stops on snow 'stead of on grass, eh. It's da first time da machine gets used for anyt'ing but ammo, an' whoever's pushin' it gets asked to do it nine times before dark wit'out once bein' offered a ride." },
  "Batting-Tee Snowman": { label: "Battin'-Tee Snowman", desc: "A snowman three feet tall gets built beside da stockpile wit' a flat top where da head'd go, an' rounds get set on it one at a time to be hit wit' da bat. Da head gets replaced forty-one times in an afternoon. Hits off da tee carry seventy feet, five more dan a round tossed up by hand, 'cause nobody's flinchin', eh. Da snowman himself gets hit twice an' he's da only ting in da yard dat don't complain." },
  "Foxhole Angel": { label: "Foxhole Angel, Eh", desc: "Somebody tries an angel at da bottom of a foxhole, two feet down an' thirty inches across, durin' a quiet hour. Da arms go nine inches before dey hit da wall, an' what's left is a body wit' stubs an' a wingspan of two feet six, which is how wide da hole is, eh. It gets counted as da first angel below da snow line. Nobody tries a second one." },
  "Sled Shortage": { label: "Not Enough Sleds, Eh", desc: "Every plastic sled on da block is eider a roof over a spreader bay or a sled now, an' dere ain't enough for both. Four of da six are on bays by noon. Da two left on da slope get ridden in turns at three minutes each, off a list pinned to a fence post, ya know. A sevent' sled turns up in a garage da second afternoon an' goes right onto a bay." },
  "Crew Mascot Snowman": { label: "Crew Mascot Snowman, Eh", desc: "Every spreader crew builds a snowman beside da bay where deir machine's kept: four feet tall, a spare wing set on his head for a hat, an' da spreader mark scratched into his front instead of his back. Da three on da crew take turns rebuildin' him. People start givin' directions by him, an' a machine left beside da wrong snowman counts as stolen, ya know. He's da first snowman dat belongs to a piece of equipment." },
  "Hill Wardens": { label: "Sleddin' Hill Wardens", desc: "Da neutral sleddin' hill gets two wardens, one from each fort, who stand at da top in fifteen-minute shifts an' wave each sled off once da run below is clear. Crashes go from four an afternoon down to none, eh. Wardens don't carry no rounds by agreement an' dey're da only ones on da block who can cross both fort lines wit'out gettin' t'rown at. Da job rotates every week an' nobody turns it down." },
  "Angel Margin": { label: "Angels Along Da Edge", desc: "Da picket crews start layin' angels into deir fresh margins, one every twelve feet, 'cause a footprint t'rough an angel's easier to see from da wall den one t'rough flat snow, eh. Ya can spot a busted angel at ninety feet, against forty for a plain track. Fourteen get made along da north margin in one afternoon. Two get found busted later by da same crews dat made 'em, walkin' back for lunch." },
  "The Rear-Room Snowman": { label: "Da Back-Room Snowman", desc: "A snowman three feet tall gets built inside da store-an'-rest room, up against da back wall, where nuttin' from outside can reach him. He's da first snowman to get t'rough a full day of fightin' wit' both stones still in place, eh. Arguments in da back room start gettin' settled facin' him, on da understandin' dat he's neutral, an' in a week of arguin' nobody's once seen him take a side." },
  "First Banked Turn": { label: "Da First Banked Turn", desc: "Dey cut a turn into da bottom of da sleddin' hill so runs quit endin' up in da trench line, banked at thirty degrees wit' a wall of packed snow two feet high on da outside. A toboggan takes it at twelve miles an hour. A saucer makes it about one time in three, an' da udder two times it goes over da wall an' stops in a trench, eh, where whichever side it landed closer to hands it back inside a minute." },
  "Angel Pages": { label: "Da Angel Pages", desc: "Da manual gives two of its twenty-two pages to angels: six feet apart at least, arms t'rough a hundred and ten degrees, an' don't use yer hands gettin' up, 'cause dat wrecks da head, eh. Da angel pages are da only ones every copy gets exactly right. T'ree centuries later da four manuscripts still around can't agree on da gate table, but dey agree on da angels right down to da degree." },
  "Snowman Waymarks": { label: "Snowman Signposts, Ya Know", desc: "Dey build eleven snowmen at da junctions between da forts, five feet tall, each one wit' a number from one to eleven laid in coal across his chest. Directions get given by 'em: two left of four, straight on past nine, eh. Number seven gets knocked down da second night an' built back facin' da wrong way, an' for a week every runner sent past him ends up at da quinzhee instead of da store." },
  "Toboggan Shed": { label: "Toboggan Shack", desc: "Dey dig a shack into da bank next to da toboggan run to keep da eight-foot toboggan outta da weather overnight: ten feet long, three high, plywood roof an' drifted over. Inside dere's a candle stub, a can of floor wax for da bottom, an' a pencil log of every run an' its time, eh. Da log hits four hundred entries in nine days. Da fastest trip down is still forty-one seconds." },
  "The Lifter": { label: "Da Lifter", desc: "Dey finally figure out how to get outta an angel widout wreckin' it: knees pulled up, a hand from somebody else, an' one long step clear from da hips. Angels made dis way keep a good head nine times outta ten, against four outta ten for somebody left to get up alone, eh. Da helper gets called da lifter. By da end of da week lifters are so busy ya gotta book 'em for an angel." },
  "Parapet Heads": { label: "Heads on Da Lip, Eh", desc: "Snowmen don't get built standin' up no more, 'cause nuttin' standin' lasts above da lip. Dey make thirty heads instead, each one eleven inches across wit' coal eyes an' a carrot, raised on sticks a foot over da parapet to draw fire. Every one gives away where whoever hits it is standin'. In da first week dey draw four hundred rounds an' find nine t'rowin' spots, an' da people raisin' an' lowerin' 'em never once look over, ya know." },
  "Runner Stockpile": { label: "Pile of Sled Runners", desc: "Da old wooden sleds come down from da rafters of three garages to make slats for da tunnels, an' a hundred and fifty feet of passage at six-foot spacin' takes eight of 'em apart. Da steel runners get kept, stacked by length behind da fort, on account of somet'ing's gonna need runners, ya know. Da plastic sleds stay on da hill an' on da bays, an' nobody fusses." },
  "Sounding Angels": { label: "Listenin' Angels", desc: "Every mornin' somebody makes an angel at da foot of every wall, 'cause a tunnel underneath shows up first as a sag in da angel's body, eh. Dey measure da sag wit' a stick laid across da wings, an' anyting over half an inch gets reported. In da first month nine sags get reported, one of 'em a tunnel an' eight of 'em just heavier people. Dey write up a rule on how heavy ya can be an' pull it da same day." },
  "Bailey Snowmen": { label: "Bailey Snowmen, Eh", desc: "Dey build fourteen snowmen in da yard of da inner bailey, seven feet tall, beside da shared keep an' way outta reach of anyting t'rown from da outer walls. Neider of da week's two assaults gets anywhere near 'em. Dey're da first snowmen in da war to last a whole season, an' deir carrots get replaced every nine days off a list pinned up by da door, da first written stock of anyting inside da walls, ya know." },
  "Strip Sled Lane": { label: "Sled Lane Between Da Walls", desc: "Dey lay a packed lane four feet wide in da strip between da two rings so ammo sleds can go da whole way around wit'out crossin' open ground. A sled loaded wit' a hundred and sixty rounds goes around da two hundred and fifty feet of outer circuit in a minute and a half. It's da safest ground in da works for sleds an' da worst for whoever's pullin' 'em, eh, so da job goes to volunteers." },
  "Countersigned Angels": { label: "Angels Wit' a Signature", desc: "Dey fix da fake-angel problem wit' a mark: a real signal angel's got a fist pressed into da snow next to da right hand, in a spot dat changes every day. Fakes drop from eleven a week to two, eh. Both sides grab da other side's schedule inside a month, an' da angels on every slope go back to meanin' nuttin' for nine days while dey draw up new schedules." },
  "Spreader-Laid Snowman": { label: "Snowman Outta Spreader Snow", desc: "A snowman gets rolled entirely outta cover da corps laid down, wit' no snow from da sky in him at all. Da base picks up sixty-one five-millimetre layers in one pass across da resurfaced lawn an' comes out three feet across, denser an' whiter dan anyting rolled before, eh. Da whole ting stands seven feet. He's da first snowman in da war made outta nuttin' dat fell, an' he takes da spreader mark on his back wit'out a crack." },
  "Cracked Sled Rule": { label: "Da Busted Sled Rule", desc: "After da first catapult takes a sled for its base, dey write a rule dat engine builders only get sleds already too busted to ride. Eleven sleds get called busted dat week, four of 'em by da builders, eh. A warden from da sleddin' hill gets put in charge of checkin' every claim against da hill's list of fourteen sleds, an' two get pulled back off engine frames still good enough to ride." },
  "Angel Squares": { label: "Angel Squares, Eh", desc: "Angels made on fresh beds, inside da hour while da snow still sticks, keep deir edges for nine days against t'ree on tromped-down ground. Da packers start leavin' a ten-foot square uncut at da end of every bed just for dat. Da square ain't in da doctrine an' nobody ever skips it once, eh. By da end of da season da front's got four hundred of 'em, every one wit' one angel in it." },
  "Snowman Assembly Line": { label: "Snowman Assembly Line, Eh", desc: "Da ammo factory sets aside one bench just for snowmen. Three crews work one after da odder, rollin' bases, middles, an' heads to size against hoops of three sizes, an' a fourth crew puts in two coals, a carrot, an' two sticks outta bins. Output settles at one finished snowman every six minutes, each one five feet tall. Da board by da door gets a third column, an' by Thursday da snowmen are ahead of both lines, ya know." },
  "Sled Shop": { label: "Da Sled Shop", desc: "A t'ird shop opens up next to da two engine shops dat only does sleds: re-rivetin' runners, patchin' cracked decks wit' heated plastic, an' puttin' new tow ropes on. Fixin' a beat-up ammo sled goes from never to a day and a half, eh. Da shop keeps eleven spare runners an' a box of rivets dat gets counted every evenin', an' it turns down engine work in writin'." },
  "Ranging Angels": { label: "Angels Ya Aim By", desc: "Dey make an angel at da foot of every rangin' stake, eight to a line out to two hundred feet, so da crews got someting to aim on when da light's bad. A standard wingspan of five feet two looks a known size at every range, an' gunners learn to read da distance off it, eh. Everybody knows da angels demselves ain't supposed to get hit. Dey get hit about once a week, an' da crew dat did it makes da angel over." },
  "Second Snowmobile": { label: "Second Snowmobile, Eh", desc: "Da owner of da first machine comes back da next mornin' wit' a neighbour's too, a newer four-stroke wit' a forty-four-inch track an' heated grips. Da two of 'em cross da front nine times before noon, eh. Hits drop from sixty-two a pass to eleven once da t'rowers figure out ya can't lead a target at t'irty miles an hour. A rulin' at lunch says neider machine is an engine, an' both owners get asked to stay off da walls." },
  "Coupling Trials": { label: "Hookin' Sleds Togedder", desc: "Dey tie two ammo sleds nose to tail wit' clothesline as a test, den three, den four, an' drag 'em out to da ravelins along da back lanes. Four's da most one runner can get goin' from a dead stop, at six hundred and forty rounds. Da knot at each hitch turns into a bowline after da first two tries wit' a granny knot leave half da load in a ditch, eh. A train's just one bigger number away now." },
  "Snowman Rearguard": { label: "Snowman Rear Guard", desc: "When dey give up two of da salients, each one gets left held by twelve snowmen posed along da walls in hats, set up overnight by da last people out. Nobody notices da pullout for two days, an' in dat time da other side puts three hundred and forty engine rounds into positions wit' nobody in 'em, eh. Da engine crews claim forty hits on a garrison dat numbered twenty-four an' was made outta snow." },
  "Sunken Sled Lanes": { label: "Sunk-Down Sled Lanes", desc: "Wit' da batteries aimin' at anyt'ing dat resupplies, da ammo sleds go below ground: lanes cut two feet deep an' three wide from da stockpile to da wall, so a loaded sled rides wit' its top layer under da lip. Losses on da run go from one sled in five to one in thirty, eh. Da lanes fill up wit' spent rounds by evenin' an' get shovelled out before dark by da ones who pull t'rough 'em." },
  "Gravity Haul": { label: "Lettin' Gravity Haul It", desc: "Where da route runs downhill toward da line, dey let da sled trains go loaded an' run by demselves, steered by one rider up front wit' a rope brake on da back sled. A train of eight does six hundred feet in under a minute wit'out a team. Da empty train gets walked back up in twelve, eh. Two outta nine end up in a wall 'stead of next to it, an' dat counts as delivered." },
  "Blockhouse Angels": { label: "Blockhouse Angels, Yah", desc: "Da blockhouse crews, wit' time on deir hands an' not many raids to deal wit', keep an angel out front of every door, made fresh after every fall. Twenty-two blockhouses keep sixty-six angels along four t'ousand feet of route, an' da sled drivers count 'em off for distance, eh. An angel missin' outside a door means trouble inside, an' dat turns out right twice da first season." },
  "Snowmobile Gun Tractor": { label: "Da Snowmobile Gun Tractor", desc: "Dey hitch a trebuchet on runners behind a snowmobile for da first time an' move it t'ree hundred feet in four minutes, 'stead of forty wit' a team of eight. Da engine rides along wit' its arm taken off an' its counterweight on a second sled, eh. Dey run da trial once by day an' once by night, an' da night run takes six minutes longer 'cause da headlight's taped over. Da batteries ask for four more machines before mornin', ya know." },
  "Runner Gauge": { label: "Runner Spacin'", desc: "Dey set one spacin' between runners for every sled, train an' engine mount on da front, at sixteen inches centre to centre, so any route grooved by one fits all da udders. Nine sleds dat don't match get rebuilt or tossed. Da routes wear two channels side by side three inches deep, eh, an' a sled wit' da wrong spacin' rides one runner high now an' tips over at da first corner." },
  "Gate Snowmen": { label: "Snowmen at Da Gate", desc: "Dey build two snowmen ten feet tall on eider side of da gap in da bailey wall where da citadel entrance is s'posed to go, a week before dere's any citadel. Each one takes six person-hours on a base ball five feet across, wit' coal eyes da size of fists an' scarves knit just for 'em, eh. Den da citadel gets laid out from dem instead of da odder way around, an' its entrance gets marked right between 'em." },
  "Citadel Snowmobile Shed": { label: "Da Snowmobile Shed at Da Citadel", desc: "Da cavalry wing gets a shed cut into da lee wall of da citadel, t'irty feet long, nine wide an' five high, wit' a door made of a hung tarp an' a floor raked level every mornin'. All seven machines fit nose to tail wit' eighteen inches between, eh. Da gas gets kept in its own cut sixty feet off, by a rule dey agreed on after one cold start filled da shed wit' smoke. Da blanketin' crews resurface da apron out front four times a day." },
  "Angel Exemption": { label: "Gettin' Outta It Wit' Angels", desc: "Dey offer a season off da roll to anybody who'll make an' keep an angel at all four block corners. Ninety-one outta da hundred an' forty sign up for sixteen spots, eh. Da angels get kept to a standard nobody's ever seen, swept twice a day an' made over after every fall, an' da fight for dose spots is worse den anyting at da front, ya know." },
  "Numbered Sleds": { label: "Sleds Wit' Numbers On", desc: "Every sled on da front gets a number painted on da deck an' wrote on da roll next to da people. Da count is two hundred and twelve: a hundred and seventy plastic, thirty wooden ones wit' steel runners, an' twelve toboggans. Each one gets assigned to a unit an' signed out every day, ya know. Inside a week da first sled gets reported missin', an' da report runs three pages." },
  "Sled Corps": { label: "Da Sled Corps", desc: "Haulin' by sled turns into its own branch of da standin' army, wit' two hundred and sixty teams of four on one roll an' its own pennant. Every train runs on a posted timetable now along da gauged routes. Da corps loses fewer people dan any udder branch an' gets chewed out da most, eh, pretty near always for ridin' da empty trains back down da hill." },
  "Pillbox Stand-Ins": { label: "Snowmen Standin' In", desc: "An inspection finds nine of da hundred and twenty pillboxes held by snowmen two feet tall, built crouchin' behind da slit, each one wit' a stick across his knees instead of a sling. Da crews posted dere built 'em before takin' off for someplace warmer, eh. Seven of da nine got reported fully manned four days runnin'. Nobody along da front noticed any change in da rate of fire from dose posts, 'cause dere never was any." },
  "Dispatch Snowmobiles": { label: "Dispatch Snowmobiles, Eh", desc: "Written orders get hauled out to da front by snowmobile, t'ree machines on a set route t'rough every battery an' every fort, at about t'irty orders a day. A run from command out to da farthest position takes a minute an' fifty seconds, near a t'ird of da six minutes from decidin' to doin'. Da riders aren't allowed to read what dey carry. Dey do anyhow, an' by da second week da front knows da orders before da officers gettin' 'em, ya know." },
  "Fort Chute": { label: "Da Fort Slide", desc: "Dey cut a slide from da t'ird story of da fort down da outside of da wall to da yard: forty feet of glazed trough at thirty degrees, ridden on a saucer or on nuttin'. It gets somebody from da top room to da ground in four seconds, against two minutes down da ladder. It gets built for gettin' out in a hurry an' gets used dat way twice, eh. For everyt'ing else it gets used about four hundred times a day." },
  "Boundary Angels": { label: "Border Angels", desc: "Between every pair of boundary markers da commission lays one angel, wingtips along da line, so ya can find da border in da dark by feel, eh. Two miles of border takes two hundred an' eleven angels. Eleven of da forty-one fights dat month come down to which side of da line some angel's left hand was on. Da commission rules on all eleven an' gets listened to on four." },
  "Relay Depots": { label: "Sled Relay Depots", desc: "Sled trains quit runnin' end to end an' start runnin' in relays between depots set every half mile behind da front. A depot holds forty sleds, a hitchin' bench an' a warmin' shack, an' a train gets broke up, loaded again an' hooked back togedder at each one in under six minutes. A round changes sleds three times now between da quarry an' da wall, eh. Da depot books are da most complete story of da front dat's left." },
  "Snowmobile Liaison": { label: "Snowmobile Liaison, Yah", desc: "Wit' da fortified line walked around an' da war spillin' into neighbourhoods dat never agreed to it, snowmobiles haul a shared timetable between seven of 'em. Four machines run a circuit of nine miles on side streets an' back yards, twice a day, an' every one signs for its copy, eh. Da timetable's kept to da minute by da riders' watches, which disagree by up to four minutes. Da first coordinated offensive starts at four different times." },
  "Pattern Snowman": { label: "Da Pattern Snowman", desc: "Snowmen get standardized to one drawin', handed out in da same folder as da engine drawin's: balls of thirty-six, twenty-six, an' eighteen inches, two coals, one carrot seven inches long, an' two sticks at forty degrees. Any head fits any body now, an' a snowman knocked apart by an engine gets put back togedder outta whatever balls are closest, eh. Dey build six hundred to da pattern in a month. A carrot da wrong length turns into an offence." },
  "Snowmobile Column Trials": { label: "Snowmobile Column Trials, Eh", desc: "Dey try da fast columns out on snowmobiles before anybody writes up any doctrine, two machines each towin' a sled of two hundred rounds over a measured quarter mile. Best time is fifty-eight seconds. Da sleds tip over on any turn tighter dan forty feet an' dump about a tent' of deir load every run, eh. Da trial report says don't put da columns on machines, 'cause dey'd outrun everyt'ing behind 'em, an' den it gets filed, ya know." },
  "Raiding Toboggans": { label: "Raidin' Toboggans", desc: "Deep raidin' parties get skinny toboggans nine feet long an' fourteen inches wide, built to get pulled single file t'rough country nobody's tracked. Each one hauls sixty rounds a head, a stove an' three days of grub, an' on any downhill da whole party of four rides, eh. Dat's how dey make nine miles a night on two hours of walkin'. Ditched raidin' toboggans are da most common t'ing found in a burned depot, an' da best proof of who burned it." },
  "Sled Weighbridge": { label: "Weighin' Da Sleds", desc: "Precision fire needs to know what it's t'rowin', so every ammo sled gets weighed on a plank scale at da depot before it goes up front. A full sled of a hundred and sixty rounds goes from sixty-one pounds to seventy-four dependin' on da snow, eh. Da number gets chalked on da deck an' copied into da battery table. A sled dat shows up not weighed gets sent back, still loaded, to da depot." },
  "Decoy Angels": { label: "Fake-Out Angels", desc: "Dey keep da decoy works over da bunker lookin' lived in, an' nuttin' looks more lived in den fresh angels, eh. A crew of four makes nine a day around da empty spots, mixin' up da wingspans from four feet to six so it looks like all kinds of people are dere. Watchers on da other side count 'em real careful an' figure a garrison of t'ree hundred. Nobody down in da bunker's ever seen one." },
  "Courtyard Snowmen": { label: "Snowmen in Da Courtyards", desc: "Wit' people livin' inside da strongholds, every closed-in yard gets a snowman of its own, an' keepin' him up turns into a household chore on a posted rota. Dey count three hundred and ten inside da bailey, each one eight feet tall, da most dat'll clear da inside doorways when ya move 'em, eh. Scarves get handed down wit' da rooms. A snowman left to slump more dan two days gets reported to da yard warden, a job made up for nuttin' else." },
  "Snowmobile Riding School": { label: "Da Snowmobile Ridin' School", desc: "Ridin' turns into a course of instruction instead of a favour from an owner: nine sessions on startin', t'rottle, formation, towin', an' gettin' a machine back out after it went t'rough a drift. T'irty riders a class learn on eleven machines dat belong to da school, eh. Da pass rate is sixty-four percent, an' most of da failures are in towin'. Da graduates are da first riders who never got let to borrow anybody else's machine, ya know." },
  "Tax Sledges": { label: "Tax Sled Trains", desc: "Da provincial tax gets paid in rounds an' delivered by sled: nine hundred a week from each of da three surplus provinces, hauled to da centre on sled trains of twelve wit' an escort. Da sleds get sealed at da provincial depot an' counted again when dey get dere, an' da difference between da two counts comes out around four percent, eh. Nobody ever gets caught for it, an' it gets budgeted for." },
  "Imperial Sled Roads": { label: "Empire Sled Roads", desc: "Forty works need haulin', so da sled routes of every province get joined into a road net of six t'ousand miles grooved to da sixteen-inch runner spacin' set on da first front. Trains of sixty sleds run it on set timetables behind teams dat swap out every eleven miles. A province on a different spacin' gets one season to regroove an' does it in nine weeks, eh. Da fort gauge comes after; da runner gauge came first." },
  "Angel Gauge": { label: "Da Angel Gauge", desc: "Da imperial gauge gets stretched to cover angels: a wingspan of five feet two, da census average, arms t'rough a hundred an' ten degrees, an' a head nine inches across. Dey lay 'em out wit' a cord an' two pegs, so ya can't tell one made in da east from one made in da west, eh. Anybody under four feet tall gets a shorter cord. Da word for an angel made by eye turns into da word for dose two forts." },
  "Imperial Snowmobile Post": { label: "Da Imperial Snowmobile Mail", desc: "Da empire runs a mail route by snowmobile out to all twenty-two enrolled settlements, on rough trails marked wit' a flag every quarter mile. A rider leaves da capital at first light every day wit' tribute receipts, orders an' private letters all in one bag, eh. Da whole round takes nine hours. Da two settlements behind on deir payments get served on da same schedule, an' da bag dat gets to 'em is always da lightest, ya know." },
  "Milecastle Snowmen": { label: "Milecastle Snowmen, Eh", desc: "Dey build a snowman outside every milecastle on da frontier wall, nineteen altogedder, each one fourteen feet tall to match da wall an' facin' out across da frontier. Every season dey get built back to da imperial gauge, in balls of seven, four and a half, an' two and a half feet, wit' coal for da eyes shipped out from da capital. Travellers crossin' at da nine gates get told to keep 'em on da left. About half do, ya know." },
  "Court Snowmobiles": { label: "Snowmobiles of Da Court", desc: "Da court keeps snowmobiles of its own, seven of 'em, one for every ward an' painted in dat ward's colour. Who goes first is set by engine size, an' da throne's machine, a six-hundred-cubic-centimetre twin, can't get passed on any lane inside da walls, eh. None of da seven ever leaves da palace. Da machines dat actually carry messages are kept in a shed by da outer wall an' aren't allowed past da first ward, ya know." },
  "Tribute Hills": { label: "Tribute Sleddin' Hills", desc: "Each client kingdom pays part of its tribute in sleddin' hills: da first run after a fresh snow on one named slope, ridden every season by da oldest kid of da imperial line in a ceremony dat lasts four minutes. Nine hills get handed over like dat. Three are under sixty feet long an' one is flat, an' da flat one gets took wit'out a word, eh, since turnin' it down would mean sayin' so." },
  "Unlicensed Sleds": { label: "Homemade Sleds, Eh", desc: "Da cartels hold every mould in da alliance except da one for a sled, which nobody ever needed. Any household can still make a sled outta a board, two runners an' a rope, an' da client kingdoms cut off from spares haul everyt'ing on 'em. Dey figure four hundred t'ousand homemade sleds in service. Da cartels apply for a licence on da design an' get told dere's nuttin' to license, ya know." },
  "Angel Clause": { label: "Da Angel Clause", desc: "Da doctrine gets a clause savin' one part in forty of every district's fresh snow for angels, same number as da engines, 'cause da one writin' it had dat number handy, eh. Sixteen of da nineteen sides go along wit' it. Da t'ree dat turned down da artillery doctrine turn dis down too an' make as many angels as dey want, which turns out to be fewer, ya know." },
  "The Snowman Question": { label: "Da Snowman Question", desc: "Dey call a fifth council to settle whedder a snowman's eyes gotta be stone, like da first ones were, or can be coal, like most of 'em been since da factory benches. It sits nineteen days. Two of its committees rule for stone, one for coal, an' one adjourns over whedder a carrot counts as part of da face, eh. Stone wins out in practice, an' da pattern of three balls, two stones, an' one stick gets written down here first." },
  "The Four-Stroke Heresy": { label: "Da Four-Stroke Heresy", desc: "Da schism gets to da snowmobile regiments its own way: can ya ride a four-stroke in a war dat a two-stroke started. Eleven regiments say ya can't, eh. Four-stroke riders get kept off da foundin' routes an' inspected at every depot, where da test is smellin' da exhaust. Da two machines dat crossed da front togedder on da second mornin', one of each, get claimed by both sides as precedent, ya know." },
  "Civic Sled Hills": { label: "Town Sleddin' Hills", desc: "Da settlement keeps eleven public sleddin' hills on its books, each one wit' a keeper, a posted schedule an' a log of every snowfall dat resurfaced it. Keepin' up da hills takes nine percent of da non-fightin' labor, more dan mappin' does, eh. Da longest public run is fourteen hundred feet. Kids under ten ride free, an' so, under a rule nobody can track down, does anybody carryin' a busted runner." },
  "Cloister Slope": { label: "Da Monastery Sleddin' Hill", desc: "Inside da monastery walls dey keep one slope for sleddin', sixty feet long at eleven degrees, resurfaced by hand off da scriptorium roof. Da sixty monks ride it once each after da first snow of da season, oldest first, on a wooden sled older dan da cloister, eh. Da run gets timed an' da time never gets wrote down. It's da only t'ing in da house dat ain't got a manual." },
  "Legend of the First Ride": { label: "Da Legend of Da First Ride", desc: "Da first snowmobile's first pass turns into a story told nine different ways. Da machine's a two-stroke in seven of 'em an' sometin' else in two, an' it gets hit by sixty-two rounds in every one, eh. In four da owner rides it, in t'ree a passenger does, an' in two nobody does. All nine agree it got took home at dark, an' da argument over whedder it counted is still bein' had in da original terms, ya know." },
  "Heir’s Angel": { label: "Da Heir's Angel", desc: "Da heir dat shows up for da first push of da season makes da season's first angel, in da swath da push just laid, before anybody else can lie down, eh. Dey measure da angel an' write da wingspan in da family register next to every one before it. Da register goes back four hundred an' twelve seasons. Da spans ain't all da same, an' da family says dey are." },
  "The Original Stones": { label: "Da Original Stones", desc: "Two grey stones get honoured as da eyes of da first real snowman, kept on a cloth in a case an' brought out once a winter to get set into a snowman built back to da original twenty-two inches. Seven settlements each got a pair. Five pairs are driveway gravel of a later grade, one pair is two different stones, an' da seventh never gets looked at, eh. Nobody claims da carrot, 'cause it got eaten." },
  "The Book of Runs": { label: "Da Book of Sled Runs", desc: "Da chroniclers keep a separate book of sled times: every trip down every timed hill in da big settlements, at about four t'ousand entries a year. It's da only record dey keep where da old stories an' da written account agree on every entry, ya know. Da fastest time on da oldest hill is older dan da book, an' both sides give it to nobody anybody can name." },
  "Snowmobile Opening Day": { label: "Snowmobile Openin' Day", desc: "Da day da trails first get groomed an' posted open turns into a set date on da calendar, eleven days after first push every year on da local count. Every regiment rides its whole strengt' over da openin' route at twenty-five miles an hour, in a column four miles long, eh. In a year when dere's no snow down by den, dey ride it anyhow, on grass, at walkin' pace, an' it goes in da record as a full openin', ya know." },
  "Funeral Toboggans": { label: "Funeral Toboggans, Ya Know", desc: "Da dead get brought to da memorials on toboggans, pulled by four an' walked at a set pace of one mile an hour no matter how far. Dey keep one toboggan just for dat at each of da sixty-one sites an' use it for nuttin' else. Da longest procession on record goes nine miles, eh. Da toboggans last longer dan da memorials, an' a bunch are older now dan anybody dey ever carried." },
  "Grave Angels": { label: "Angels Over Da Graves", desc: "Over every burial somebody makes an angel da next winter an' every winter after dat, whoever lives closest. Diggers find da pressed layer of every one kept in da firn as a thin hard sheet, so one grave can have two hundred an' forty angels stacked on top, eh. Dey use da stacks to date da burials. Dey're more reliable den da written record, which don't even exist yet." },
  "Snowmobile Warlords": { label: "Da Snowmobile Warlords", desc: "Every one of da nine short dynasties gets started on a park of snowmobiles, an' most of 'em end when da park runs outta gas. Da biggest musters a hundred an' forty machines an' holds a reach of two miles for nineteen hours, eh. Machines change hands faster dan capitals do, an' one four-stroke's on record under six different owners in a day. Da machines outlast every line dat rode 'em an' at da end dey're counted as da only holdin's dat stayed put." },
  "Snowman Wrights": { label: "Da Snowman Wrights", desc: "Buildin' snowmen turns into a licensed trade in da castle towns, wit' masters, apprentices, a seven-year term, an' a set fee for every foot of height. Nineteen towns license a hundred and forty wrights between 'em. Shopkeepers who build deir own outside deir shops get fined for it, eh. Da wrights keep up da old-timer sites, roll da market-square snowmen, an' refuse all togedder to build for da warlords, who pay twice da fee to get it done anyhow." },
  "Hill Tolls": { label: "Sleddin' Hill Tolls", desc: "In da collapse, a hill belongs to whoever can stand at da top of it. Dey count thirty-one tolls on da old public runs, paid in rounds at rates from four a trip down to forty. Da hill registry makes it t'rough in one piece an' nobody pays it any mind, eh. Da longest claim dat never broke belongs to a keeper wit' no machines, no fort an' one toboggan, on a hill none of da nine warlords ever bothered to take." },
  "The First Rider": { label: "Da First One on a Saucer", desc: "Da old foundin' stories say da first saucer ride crossed da whole territory in one afternoon an' only stopped where da snow gave out. Da number thirty-one feet is still in da story, as how many times da saucer spun around. Nine settlements claim da slope it started from, eh. None of da nine has a slope of nine degrees, an' all nine went an' built one." },
  "Swath Angels": { label: "Big Swath Angels", desc: "Every one of da nine big engines gets its first swath finished off wit' an angel made to da size of da machine: a wingspan of ninety-two feet, worked by forty people lyin' in da outline an' sweepin' togedder, eh. Da proportions match da standard angel to t'ree decimal places. Four of da angels get written down. Of da four engines still standin' as monuments, nobody can say for sure which angel goes wit' which." },
  "Snowmobile Registry": { label: "Da Snowmobile Registry", desc: "Da scribes start a snowmobile registry, one line for every machine: number, regiment, track lengt', an' da machine it got rebuilt from. Four t'ousand one hundred entries go in da first year, eh. Every line of descent gets traced back toward dat borrowed two-stroke, an' t'ree hundred an' eleven of 'em make it. Da rest go in as comin' from da foundin' engine by tradition, which da registry keeps as its own column, ya know." },
  "Terrace Snowmen": { label: "Snowmen on Da Terraces", desc: "Dey set a snowman at da gate of every terrace on da step fortress, nine altogedder, each one ten feet taller dan da one below, from nine feet at da bottom gate up to eighty-nine on da summit platform. Da scribes write down every rebuildin', four hundred and twelve entries over nineteen years. 'Cause da gates don't line up, ya can't see more dan two of 'em from anyplace on da fortress, eh, so attackers count 'em to know how far dey still gotta go." },
  "The Run Survey": { label: "Surveyin' Da Big Run", desc: "Before anybody even brings up an armistice, every slope in reach of da highest rampart gets surveyed for a run as big as da engines. Dey measure eleven routes. Da one dey pick drops four hundred and ten feet over four miles to da river flats an' needs nine banked turns, each one walled to da classical proportions on account of dose hold, eh. Da survey gets filed wit' da codex, an' nobody says yet what it's for." },
  "Armistice Snowmobile Races": { label: "Armistice Snowmobile Races, Eh", desc: "Wit' da long peace on, da regiments race. Da big one is a ninety-mile course over da civil roads da spreaders lay every mornin', run once a year by a field of sixty machines in full regiment colours. Da winnin' time drops from t'ree hours ten to two hours seventeen over four decades, eh. Both sides know a regiment dat can win da race can also cross a province in an afternoon, an' both sides enter every year, ya know." },
  "The Neutral Run": { label: "Da Big Run Stays Neutral", desc: "A season before da territory falls apart, da Big Run gets declared outside every jurisdiction by an agreement signed by all five of what are about to be separate governments. Da four miles an' nine turns get marked wit' blue stakes every forty feet, eh. When da borders get drawn, two of 'em cross da run, an' both stop at da stakes an' pick up again on da far side." },
  "Charter Angels": { label: "Claim Angels", desc: "A claim ain't legal till somebody born back home makes an angel at its charter post. Thirty-one get made da first season, every one written down wit' its wingspan an' da name of da boat, eh. Outposts dat lose contact keep makin' 'em every winter, an' at t'ree of 'em da angels get found a century later wit' deir heads still pointed at a capital dat's moved four hundred miles since." },
  "Charter Sledges": { label: "Charter Sled Trains", desc: "Each outpost heads out behind a sled train of forty sleds haulin' its eight t'ousand rounds, its engine in pieces, an' a toboggan off da Big Run for da first good slope it finds. Da sleds make twelve miles a day, an' da farthest charter post gets reached on da fourt'. Eleven outposts lose contact, eh. In spring three of deir toboggans come back down da river by demselves, empty." },
  "Forward Observer Snowmobiles": { label: "Snowmobile Spotters Out Front", desc: "Firin' past da horizon needs somebody at da far end, so spotters get sent out by snowmobile two to four miles ahead of da batteries to report where da rounds land. Every machine carries a rider, a range card an' a signal lamp, eh. Wit' ninety seconds of flight time, a spotter hears a round come in before seein' it, a lot of da time. Losses run high, near all of 'em from deir own side's fire, which still lands only one round in forty where it was s'posed to." },
  "Survey Snowmen": { label: "Survey Snowmen, Eh", desc: "Dey build a snowman at da corner of every numbered swath in da blanket grid, one for every hundred square miles, four thousand altogedder, as markers ya can read from a pass wit'out stoppin'. Each one stands twenty feet an' carries his swath number in coal across da middle ball. Da grid lays over 'em on schedule at five millimetres a pass, so every year dey get whiter an' a little bigger, an' da oldest are taller now dan da survey says, ya know." },
  "Level Chutes": { label: "Sled Chutes T'rough Da Levels", desc: "Da arcology's got sled chutes all t'rough it, a spiral trough in each of nineteen stairwells runnin' all two hundred and forty levels from da roof down to da quarries. Somebody on a saucer gets from da top to da bottom in six minutes. Da lifts take forty, eh. Da chutes are da only way t'rough da buildin' da fight between levels never touches, since nobody rides 'em up." },
  "Siege Ring Snowmobiles": { label: "Snowmobiles Ringin' Da Siege", desc: "Da besiegers keep da siege shut tight wit' a ring of snowmobiles ridin' da outside line, a circuit of fourteen miles, wit' a machine goin' past every spot every six minutes. Over eight hundred an' forty days da ring logs nineteen million miles an' wears t'rough seventeen t'ousand tracks, eh. It swaps out its riders more often dan eider garrison gets swapped. Nuttin' gets out, an' by da end nuttin's tryin', ya know." },
  "Keepers of the Run": { label: "Keepers of Da Big Run", desc: "Da Big Run still gets resurfaced every mornin' like it was built, by families who ain't done nuttin' else for nine generations. A keeper gets trained from age six on da nine banked turns, one turn a year, an' ain't let near da top till fifteen. Da record of four minutes eleven seconds still stands, eh. Keepers ain't allowed to ride it, an' far as da record goes, none of 'em ever asked." },
  "Roof Angels": { label: "Angels Up On Da Roof", desc: "Da cathedral machines lay a bed on da flat parts of da roof every dawn, an' a keeper climbs a hundred an' fifty steps to make one angel in it. Da roof angels are da highest in da world, ya can't see 'em from da ground, an' dey get made anyway, eh. Nine hundred years of keepers make t'ree hundred an' twenty-eight t'ousand of 'em, every one laid over da last. Nobody tells da keepers why, an' dey don't ask." },
  "Niche Snowmen": { label: "Snowmen in Da Niches", desc: "Da ice cathedrals get snowmen instead of statues: four hundred niches along da walls of da nave, each one holdin' a snowman of three balls at twelve feet, wit' eyes of polished coal an' a stick in each hand. Dey get carved instead of rolled, an' glazed wit' da walls every season, eh. Who each one stands for gets lettered on da plinth. Two hundred and nine of da plinths are blank, an' dose niches get da most visitors." },
  "The Snowmobile Guild": { label: "Da Snowmobile Guild", desc: "Da mechanics who keep da snowmobile park runnin' get organised into a guild, an' it claims it comes down from da crews who kept da first regiment depots goin'. Ya get in by seven years of apprenticeship an' bein' able to set a carburettor by ear, eh. Da guild's got da only full set of shop manuals an' lends out pages, never volumes. Da spreader houses each try to bring it under 'em an' fail, 'cause none of 'em can keep deir own machines runnin' wit'out it." },
  "Gallery Haulage": { label: "Sled Haulin' Under Da Ice", desc: "Below da surface, everyt'ing dat moves t'rough da galleries moves on sleds: flat sleds wit' steel runners, pulled by crews of three over floors da machines down dere laid. A sled hauls nine hundred pounds at walkin' speed an' never gets brought up eider, eh. Da galleries get built to sled width, eleven feet, an' da oldest sled still workin' has outlasted three generations of crew." },
  "Ceiling Angels": { label: "Angels On Da Ceilin'", desc: "Down in da interior dere's no open snow to lie on, so dey carve angels into da chamber ceilin's instead, cut from below by a mason on a ladder to da outline of somebody lyin' up top, eh. Four hundred chambers got nine t'ousand of 'em. Kids raised underground get taught every one's da print of somebody lyin' on da surface, an' for da oldest few dat's true." },
  "Ice-Bore Runs": { label: "Toboggan Runs Under Da Ice", desc: "Sleddin' goes under da sheet wit' everyt'ing else: runs bored at a steady one and a half degrees t'rough da ice between chambers, da longest one eleven miles, ridden on toboggans wit' steel runners at da old sixteen-inch spacin'. A trip down between da two deepest works takes nineteen minutes. Da climb back takes four days, eh, so traffic goes one way an' da toboggans get hauled back up in trains." },
  "Snowmobile Passage Couriers": { label: "Snowmobile Couriers T'rough Da Passage", desc: "Da nine-day trip t'rough neutral passage between da two farthest-apart peoples gets cut to four by snowmobile, on a groomed lane t'rough ice dat belongs to neider one. Da couriers come from neider people an' ride under a neutral colour, eh. Every one carries messages in both dialects an' in a t'ird one da couriers worked out amongst demselves, which da two peoples started usin' wit' each udder. Twenty-two couriers hold da route, ya know." },
  "Snowman Wells": { label: "Snowman Wells, Eh", desc: "While da sheet rises over da old-timer sites, every one gets kept open as a shaft down to da original ground so da snowman can still get built on da same spot every winter. Sixty-three of da ninety-one make it as wells, da deepest a hundred and forty feet, lined wit' steps. Da builders carry da stones down by hand an' lower da stick on a cord, ya know. No daylight's reached da snowman at da bottom of da deepest well in three hundred years." },
  "The Spiral Chute": { label: "Da Spiral Slide", desc: "Dey cut a sled chute down da wall of da shaft keep in a spiral, two thirds of a mile deep, so somebody at da surface gets down to da command level at da bottom wit'out usin' one floor. Da trip down takes eleven minutes on a toboggan. Somebody takin' da keep floor by floor would need three weeks, eh. Da chute's been sealed at da top since da day it opened, for exactly dat reason." },
  "Storm Survey Snowmobiles": { label: "Storm Survey Snowmobiles, Eh", desc: "Wit' da cryosphere makin' its own weat'er, snowmobiles go out after every storm to measure what it left: dept', density an' drift every mile across a survey grid four hundred miles on a side. Forty-one storms in a year keep sixty survey crews out dere wit'out a break, eh. Da surveys find a t'ird of da new surface got laid by machines instead of fallin', an' by da next spring da survey office can't tell da difference no more, ya know." },
  "The Polar Descent": { label: "Da Long Polar Slide", desc: "A sled run gets laid across da whole polar sheet on da albedo schedule, nine hundred miles long an' droppin' eleven t'ousand feet from da dome down to da coast. Riders climb on in groups of forty an' get dere two days later wit'out ever pushin' off twice, ya know. It's da only line on da coverage map drawn for some reason udder dan temperature, an' da office dat sets da cold redraws it every year." },
  "The Angel Article": { label: "Da Angel Article", desc: "Article six hundred an' twelve of da charter spells out da angel all da way an' gives everybody da right to make one every winter on surface ground. Ninety-six percent of folks live down below an' gotta apply for a surface pass to do it, an' eleven million passes go out da first year, eh. Da last independent fort only signs on once its own angels, a quarter inch skinnier, get recognised." },
  "Stacked Sentries": { label: "Sentries Stacked Up", desc: "Every story of da hundred-story fort has got two snowmen at da top of its ramp, four feet tall an' facin' out, 'cause da drawin' of da two-story original shows sentries dere. Dat makes two hundred, kept up by a standin' crew of eleven who work down from da top floor over nineteen days an' den start all over, eh. Not one's ever been shot at. On da top floor da pair look out a thousand feet over da front at nuttin' in range." },
  "Equatorial Snowmobile Lane": { label: "Da Equator Snowmobile Lane", desc: "Da top of da equator wall, fifty feet across, gets groomed as one snowmobile lane twenty-four t'ousand nine hundred miles long, da only road on da planet wit' no end to it. Relays ride it bot' directions wit' a station every forty miles, eh. A whole circuit takes sixty-one days. Which edge of da lane is da outside is set by da charter an' flips wit' da century, so da riders' rule is just keep to da middle, ya know." },
  "Tether Sledges": { label: "Freight Sleds Down Da Tether", desc: "Freight comes down da orbital fort on sleds ridin' da outside of da tether, twenty-two t'ousand two hundred and thirty-six miles on braked runners at a steady four hundred miles an hour. Da trip takes fifty-six hours. Dey don't carry no riders, 'cause nobody's figured out how to stop da last mile gentle, eh. Da brakin' record from dose sleds is what da first sled wit' a rider comin' down from orbit gets designed around." },
  "Scheduled Reentry": { label: "Toboggan Down From Orbit on Schedule", desc: "Sleddin' down from orbit turns into a timetable: two-hundred-foot toboggans let go from orbit four times a day, each one comin' down on runners at da same polar station inside half a mile. It lands better dan droppin' snow from orbit ever did, on account of you can steer a toboggan an' you can't steer a slug, eh. Two t'ousand riders a year use it an' nine hundred and eighty outta every t'ousand make it, against nine outta eleven on da first tries." },
  "Ring Track Snowmobiles": { label: "Snowmobiles on Da Ring Track", desc: "Upkeep on da orbit rings gets done by snowmobile, run along da outside face of every ring on a groomed track dat follows da screw end to end. A crew of two clears jammed flights an' reseats wing panels on a beat of nine hundred miles, eh. Forty machines cover da t'ree rings. Da riders are da only people who've seen dat dusk line from da ground an' from on top bot', an' dey say from on top it looks like a trail, ya know." },
  "Doorman in Orbit": { label: "Da Doorman Up in Orbit", desc: "Dey build a snowman beside da entrance tunnel of da orbital igloo at a hundred times da size of da first real snowman, a hundred and eighty-three feet in three balls, 'cause da one person runnin' it read dat a snowman stood by da original. Wit' no gravity to stack against, da balls get cabled t'rough da middle. His eyes are captured chunks eleven feet across, eh. Da operator's da only person ever to see him from closer dan forty miles." },
  "Front-Line Angels": { label: "Angels On Da Front Line", desc: "Both commands keep a line of angels along deir side of da equator front, one every mile, heads pointed home, to show who's holdin' it. Fifty t'ousand get kept up between da two hemispheres, eh. At four spots da lines are close enough to reach, an' dere da angels get made wit' fingertips almost touchin' across da line, by a deal dey renew every winter for a decade." },
  "Universal Sled Issue": { label: "A Sled for Everybody", desc: "Wit' no rear area left, every one of da four hundred million enrolled gets issued a sled: a thirty-inch moulded deck, a tow rope an' a pair of runners at da old sixteen-inch spacin'. It's da only piece of gear both sides hand out to da same pattern. It hauls rounds, da wounded an' da dead, an' on any slope wit' a few minutes free it gets ridden down, eh, which neider side has managed to stop." },
  "Pressure-Launched Toboggan": { label: "Air-Shot Toboggan", desc: "Dey tap da compressed-air tanks dat run da batteries to get sleds goin' too, shootin' a twelve-person toboggan up a ramp onto da sheet at four hundred miles an hour. Den it slides wit' no power for three hundred miles. One tank charge does forty runs, eh. Da launch tube's da only piece of pressure artillery ever pointed away from da enemy on purpose, an' it fires more often dan any battery on da sheet." },
  "Meridian Snowmobile Run": { label: "Da Meridian Snowmobile Run", desc: "One route gets groomed from da pole down to da equator along da line da resurfacin' works follow, six t'ousand two hundred miles of packed lane alongside da stuff headin' sout'. Riders run it as a relay in nineteen days, eh. Mostly it's crews checkin' da works dat ride it, an' once a year a field of four hundred races it. Da record, set early an' never beat, is eleven days, by a team dat didn't stop to check nuttin', ya know." },
  "Unattended Angels": { label: "Angels Wit' Nobody Around", desc: "One long-range flight over a sector nobody can reach finds da bed laid even, like everybody figured, an' someting nobody figured: angels six feet apart in rows of four, every one at da standard span, along ninety miles of swath, eh. Nobody's seen. Da flight don't land. Da sector goes into da census as t'ree hundred an' seventeen t'ousand angels, makers unknown." },
  "Lunar Snowman": { label: "Snowman on Da Moon", desc: "Da first snowman off da planet gets built on da moon, ahead of da crater fort, by a survey crew wit' snow hauled up in sealed drums. In a sixth of da gravity da balls stack up wit'out settlin', so he goes up nine feet on a base only two feet across an' stays dat way, eh. Da carrot's freeze-dried an' da stones are local. Wit' no air an' no weather, he's gonna outlast everyting on da planet he got carried from." },
  "Tethered Snowmobiles": { label: "Snowmobiles on a Leash", desc: "On da four garrisoned orbit positions, chunks of packed ice a few miles across, snowmobiles get run on cable. Escape velocity out dere is under five miles an hour, so every machine's clipped to a steel line strung around da body an' rides it like a streetcar, eh. Top speed is t'ree miles an hour. Nineteen machines serve da four positions, an' da one dat came off its line da first year can still be seen from t'ree of 'em, ya know." },
  "Comet Run": { label: "Sleddin' on a Comet", desc: "Dey lay a run down da longest side of a comet nucleus nine miles long, where dere's so little gravity a toboggan pushed off at walkin' speed takes eleven hours to get to da bottom. Riders get tied to da runners. It's da longest trip down ever timed an' da slowest, eh, an' da run log shows more people sleepin' at da finish dan awake." },
  "The Dome Run": { label: "Slidin' Inside Da Comet Dome", desc: "Dey lay a run around da inside of da comet quinzhee, spiralin' down da hollowed-out wall from da crown to da floor six miles down. Wit' dat gravity a toboggan needs four days to finish it an' gets passed, on da way, by everyt'ing it was loaded wit', eh. Formations inside take turns on it by allegiance. When three are dere it's da only part of da dome all three agree to share." },
  "Centennial Angels": { label: "Once-a-Century Angels", desc: "Out at da outer front every formation makes one angel a century, in da same spot, on da anniversary of da line gettin' drawn. Forty are on record from each side, eh. Since da ground moves eleven inches a century one way or da other, da angels make a little scatter, da widest pair eight feet apart, an' dat's da best record of da line dere is, cited in about a t'ird of da ninety-six cases a year." },
  "Girdle Patrol Snowmobiles": { label: "Snowmobiles Patrollin' Da Girdle", desc: "Every girdle spreader's got a snowmobile track along its trough, eleven t'ousand miles of it, ridden by patrols lookin' for anyt'ing dat might stop da screw. Dey never found nuttin', eh. A patrol covers a quarter of da way around in one four-day turn of da screw an' hands off to da next. Ninety riders serve da four girdles. Deir standin' orders say don't touch da screw, an' da unwritten ones say don't walk in front of it, ya know." },
  "Unattended Snowmen": { label: "Snowmen Nobody's Watchin'", desc: "Da copied works start buildin' snowmen beside deir own doors, three balls wit' two coals an' two sticks, 'cause da copied drawin's for a spreader bay still show one standin' dere. No order ever covered it an' nobody can find one to stop it. Da last survey counts nineteen thousand, every one four feet tall wit' da spreader mark on his front, eh. Da carrots get left off, since no drawin' says where a carrot comes from." },
  "The Sled Canon": { label: "Da Sled Canon, Eh", desc: "Every sled in da war, at any size, is one of three kinds set down in da deep record: da saucer at twenty-six inches, da toboggan at eight feet, an' da runner sled at sixteen-inch spacin', each one made bigger but never changed. Somebody proposes a fourt' kind eleven times in nine t'ousand years. Every proposal gets filed under volume nine, which is lost, an' so da canon holds, ya know." },
  "The Hill Register": { label: "Da Sleddin' Hill Register", desc: "Da register of sleddin' hills dat got started when dere were thirty-four is still kept, up to nine hundred million entries now across every body wit' a sheet, each one namin' da line dat gets da first run after a fresh snow. Most of da lines died out an' deir entries get kept anyway, eh. Da oldest entry, a run of six hundred feet, can't be found on any world no more, an' its first run is still wrote down as owed." },
  "Starlight Snowmobiles": { label: "Starlight Snowmobiles, Eh", desc: "Snowmobiles built for da star-driven works get deir drive from a collector, a film sail four hundred feet across dat turns da track as long as da light holds. On da sunny side ice of da outer bodies dey make nine miles an hour, eh. Dey stop da second da sail gets shaded, which is da original rule put on a machine dat never had it. Da handbook tells riders keep da star behind ya an' da shadow out front, ya know." },
  "Posthumous Angels": { label: "Angels for Da Long Gone", desc: "Da order to make an angel when every new head of da order takes over gets to da farthest garrison four hundred years late, an' dey do it just like it's written, wingspan to da inch, eh. At any time eleven of dose orders are on da way. Da far garrisons make angels for heads of da order dead a long time, in order, about one every thirty-six years, an' keep 'em in a row widout sayin' nuttin'." },
  "Reported Snowmen": { label: "Snowmen on Da Report", desc: "Sixty-one standin' positions report, right on schedule, dat da snowman at da gate is upright an' in one piece, same as every position's reported since da form first got drawn up. Da reports take four thousand years to get here an' tell about snowmen at positions nobody alive has ever been to. One report in nine mentions a replaced stick, eh. Not one's ever mentioned a replaced stone, an' da archive takes dat as fittin' wit' doctrine." },
  "Snowmobile Embarkation": { label: "Loadin' Up Da Snowmobiles", desc: "A snowmobile regiment of four hundred machines gets loaded onto a slow ship for a system sixteen light-years off, where da coordinates say an enemy might be. Every machine gets gassed up, idled for nine minutes an' chocked in da hold, an' da regiment colours go on last, eh. Nobody's seen da enemy in eleven hundred years. Da loadin' order says so, an' gives an arrival date a hundred an' sixty years out, ya know." },
  "Transfer Toboggans": { label: "Moon-to-Moon Toboggans", desc: "Toboggans get run between moons on transfer orbits: a push off one surface an' a landin' on runners at anudder one nine months later. Each one hauls a crew of six an' four hundred tons of pack from wherever it runs t'ickest. Da fleet's up to eleven t'ousand, an' every landin' strip gets resurfaced to five millimetres ahead of each one comin' in, eh, 'cause a toboggan of any size stops best on snow." },
  "Inheritor Toboggans": { label: "Toboggans Da Newcomers Found", desc: "Each of da three peoples dat inherited da line finds da toboggans in da positions dey took over an' starts usin' 'em wit'out anybody showin' 'em how. All three ride 'em down da closest slope after a fresh snow, oldest kid first, whedder or not dat kid can steer. None of da three can say why, eh. It's da only custom da three share, an' each one figures da udder two copied it." },
  "The Last Saucer": { label: "Da Last Saucer", desc: "Past every front, near da end of da measured scale, somebody carries a plastic saucer twenty-six inches across to da top of a slope of nine degrees an' pushes off. It goes thirty-one feet before stoppin' dead on a bare patch, spinnin' once on da way. Da second run follows da same track to da same patch, eh. Nobody writes down who rode it, an' it gets ridden eleven times before dark." },
  "The Last Angel": { label: "Da Last Angel", desc: "Before da afternoon's done, one of da t'ree lies down in da scraped circle next to da last pile, where a little over an eighth of an inch is left, an' sweeps both arms t'rough a hundred an' ten degrees four times. It comes out green on white, wit' a wingspan of five feet one, eh. Ya can see it for nineteen minutes an' it counts, by unanimous rulin' of da other two, as an angel." },
  "Snowman on the Crown": { label: "Snowman Up on Da Crown", desc: "Up on da crown of da Axis Keep, nine hundred miles over da yard, dere's a snowman twenty-two inches tall in three balls, wit' two stones an' a carrot cut down by a third, built to da measurements of da first real snowman. He's da only ting on da keep not built to da Classical proportion, eh. He's never been resurfaced, 'cause nuttin's ever reached da crown to do it, an' he's da smallest ting eider side ever agreed not to shoot at." },
  "The Keep Descent": { label: "Da Long Slide Down Da Keep", desc: "Dey lay a run down da sout' side of da Axis Keep, four t'ousand miles from da top to da bottom, da only slope ever built where a sled can't finish before da snow under it needs resurfacin'. A trip down takes nineteen years. Riders climb on as kids an' get dere as da oldest ones on board, ya know. It got pushed off once at da top, by hand, an' nuttin's pushed it since." },
  "The Parked Snowmobile": { label: "Da Parked Snowmobile", desc: "At da line dat don't move dey keep one snowmobile, da last machine on eider side dat coulda crossed it, an' da track's been took off it. It sits a yard back of da boundary on a groomed apron, gassed up, started once a quarter for nine minutes, an' logged in bot' sides' returns as operational, eh. Nobody suggests ridin' it. Its pull cord's a replacement of a replacement of da one in da archive, an' it still works, ya know." }
});
